(function(){
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(w,origin)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const Q=(id,senseId,errorType,prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain)=>({id,senseId,type:'辨義與用法',errorType,prompt,options:[answer,d1,d2],answer,explain});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistakes,quiz)=>D(w,{etymology:E(w,origin),contexts,mistakes,quiz});
P('variant','From Latin variantem, present participle of variare, “change”; a variant differs from a usual form.',[C('variant.s1','不同形式','The blue variant of the chair uses a darker fabric but keeps the same frame.','這張椅子的藍色款使用較深的布料，但保留相同框架。','a variant of + product / design','Noun: a form that is slightly different from the usual type.','The chair is one altered version of the usual design.'),C('variant.s2','词形变体','“Colour” is a British spelling variant of “color.”','“Colour”是“color”的英式拼字變體。','a spelling / word variant','Noun: a slightly different form of a word, product, or design.','The spelling differs while the word remains the same.'),C('variant.s3','病毒变种','Scientists compared the new virus variant with earlier samples to track mutations.','科學家把新病毒變種與早期樣本比較，以追蹤突變。','a virus variant','Noun: a changed form of a virus that spreads after mutation.','Mutations have produced a changed viral form.')],[M('“Colour” is a variant spelling of “color,” but the two spellings are identical in every letter.','“Colour” is a variant spelling of “color,” with an extra u.','The spellings differ: British colour includes an extra u.')],[Q('variant.q1','variant.s1','meaning','How does the blue chair variant differ?','It uses darker fabric but keeps the same frame.','It is the exact same chair in every detail.','It is a new virus mutation.','A variant is a slightly changed form of a usual type.'),Q('variant.q2','variant.s2','context','Why is “colour” called a spelling variant?','It is a different spelling of the same word.','It is a new kind of chair.','It is a virus that spreads by mutation.','A word variant is a changed form of a word.'),Q('variant.q3','variant.s3','distinction','What are scientists tracking in the new virus variant?','Mutations that produced a changed viral form.','Changes in chair fabric.','British spelling differences.','A virus variant is a form changed by mutation.'),Q('variant.q4','variant.s1','word-choice','Choose the product use of variant.','A lighter variant of the same backpack design.','A variant spelling of a word.','A variant virus found in samples.','The backpack is a slightly different product form.')]);
P('variation','From Latin variationem, “change or difference,” based on variare, “make different.”',[C('variation.s1','变化幅度','Daily variation in the river level depends on rainfall upstream.','河流水位每日的變化取決於上游降雨。','variation in + amount / level / form','Noun: a change in amount, level, or form.','The river level changes from day to day.'),C('variation.s2','不同形式','The museum displays a winter variation of the same landscape, painted in pale colours.','博物館展示同一幅風景畫的冬季版本，色彩較淡。','a variation of + design / theme','Noun: a different form of the same thing.','The painting retains the subject but changes its appearance.'),C('variation.s3','音乐变奏','The pianist repeated the melody in a slow variation with altered rhythm.','鋼琴家以節奏改變的慢速變奏重複了旋律。','a variation on + musical theme','Noun: a musical theme repeated with changed rhythm or notes.','The central melody is recognizable but modified.')],[M('The pianist played a variation of the melody without changing a single note or its rhythm.','The pianist played the melody without variation, keeping every note and rhythm unchanged.','A variation changes at least some notes, rhythm, or form.')],[Q('variation.q1','variation.s1','meaning','What does daily variation describe?','Changes in the river’s level from day to day.','The same level every day.','A painting’s winter version.','This sense concerns change in an amount or level.'),Q('variation.q2','variation.s2','context','What is the winter painting?','A different form of the same landscape.','A completely unrelated musical theme.','A measurement of river depth.','A variation is a changed form of the same thing.'),Q('variation.q3','variation.s3','distinction','What did the pianist alter in the variation?','The melody’s rhythm while repeating its theme.','The museum’s painting frame.','The river level upstream.','Musical variation changes notes or rhythm of a theme.'),Q('variation.q4','variation.s1','word-choice','Which phrase refers to a difference in quantity?','variation in monthly rainfall','a variation on the same melody','a winter variation of the landscape','The first concerns an amount that changes.')]);
P('varicolored','From vari- (various) + colored, describing something marked with several colours.',[C('varicolored.s1','多种颜色','The varicolored kite had red, yellow, and green panels that flashed in the sun.','這只多色風箏有紅、黃、綠三色面板，在陽光下閃耀。','varicolored + object / pattern','Adjective: marked or decorated with a variety of colours.','The kite has multiple distinct colours.')],[M('The varicolored flag was painted in a single uniform shade with no other colour.','The monochrome flag was painted in a single uniform shade.','An object with only one shade is monochrome, not varicolored.')],[Q('varicolored.q1','varicolored.s1','meaning','What did the varicolored kite look like?','It had red, yellow, and green panels.','It was a single uniform shade.','It had no colour at all.','Varicolored means marked with several colours.'),Q('varicolored.q2','varicolored.s1','context','Which bird would be varicolored?','A bird with several different colours across its feathers.','A bird whose feathers are all one shade.','A bird hidden in a dark room.','The adjective describes multiple colours.'),Q('varicolored.q3','varicolored.s1','distinction','What is the opposite of a varicolored design here?','A plain design in one colour.','A patchwork of several colours.','A multicolour striped pattern.','One uniform shade contrasts with many colours.'),Q('varicolored.q4','varicolored.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate description.','a varicolored mosaic of blue, gold, and white tiles','a varicolored wall painted entirely white','a varicolored cloth with no dye or pattern','The mosaic uses several colours.')]);
P('varied','From vary + -ed, describing many types or differences in shape, size, or quality.',[C('varied.s1','多样','The festival offered a varied programme of music, workshops, and outdoor films.','藝術節提供多樣化的節目，包括音樂、工作坊和戶外電影。','a varied selection / programme / diet','Adjective: consisting of many different types of thing.','The schedule includes several kinds of activities.'),C('varied.s2','彼此不同','The samples were varied in size, from tiny grains to large smooth stones.','樣本大小各異，從細小顆粒到大型光滑石塊都有。','varied in + size / shape / quality','Adjective: different from one another in shape, size, or quality.','Individual samples do not share one size.')],[M('The varied programme contained only one identical activity repeated every hour.','The uniform programme contained one identical activity repeated every hour.','A programme with only one repeated activity is not varied.')],[Q('varied.q1','varied.s1','meaning','Why was the festival programme varied?','It included music, workshops, and films.','It repeated one activity only.','It listed only music.','Varied can mean made up of different kinds.'),Q('varied.q2','varied.s2','context','How were the samples varied?','They differed in size and texture.','Every sample was exactly alike.','They were all the same large stone.','This sense means different from one another.'),Q('varied.q3','varied.s1','distinction','Which menu is varied?','A menu with soups, salads, grains, and fruit.','A menu offering the same soup at every meal.','A menu listing one item only.','It consists of many different types of food.'),Q('varied.q4','varied.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about items differing from one another.','varied in shape and size','a varied selection of sports','a varied programme of events','The first describes differences among items.')]);
P('variety','From Latin varietas, “difference or diversity,” based on varius, “different.”',[C('variety.s1','多样性','The variety of tasks kept the research assistants interested throughout the summer.','工作的多樣性讓研究助理整個夏天都保持興趣。','a variety of + plural noun','Noun: the quality of including many different types of thing.','The tasks are not all the same.'),C('variety.s2','品种','This variety of apple stays crisp after baking and is often used in pies.','這種蘋果品種烘烤後仍然爽脆，常用來做派。','a variety of + plant / product','Noun: a particular type of plant, animal, or product differing from others of its kind.','It is one distinct kind among apple varieties.')],[M('The variety of tasks meant the assistants repeated the same identical task all summer.','The uniformity of tasks meant the assistants repeated the same task all summer.','Repeating one identical task describes uniformity, not variety.')],[Q('variety.q1','variety.s1','meaning','What kept the assistants interested?','The tasks included different kinds of work.','They repeated only one task all summer.','They stopped working in spring.','Variety is the quality of having many different types.'),Q('variety.q2','variety.s2','context','What kind of apple is described?','A particular type that stays crisp when baked.','All apple trees in the world.','A music programme.','A variety is a distinct type within a larger kind.'),Q('variety.q3','variety.s1','distinction','Which phrase means “a range of different items”?','a variety of local dishes','one single dish served every day','a single named apple cultivar','The phrase indicates multiple kinds of dishes.'),Q('variety.q4','variety.s2','word-choice','Choose the botanical sense.','a variety of rose resistant to frost','a variety of activities at a fair','a variety of opinions in a discussion','The first names a particular type of plant.')]);
P('various','From Latin varius, “different or changeable,” through Old French; it means several different kinds or more than one across a range.',[C('various.s1','不同种类','The archive holds various maps, letters, and photographs from the expedition.','檔案館收藏了探險隊的各種地圖、信件和照片。','various + plural noun','Adjective: several different kinds, not all the same.','The collection contains distinct categories.'),C('various.s2','多于一个','Several residents gave various reasons for opposing the closure.','幾位居民提出了不同理由反對關閉。','various + plural item, viewed as a range','Adjective: more than one, considered across a range.','The word signals multiple reasons or items.')],[M('The archive held various maps, but every map was an identical copy of the same sheet.','The archive held a single map, copied many times from the same sheet.','Identical copies do not constitute various different kinds of maps.')],[Q('various.q1','various.s1','meaning','What did the archive contain?','Different kinds of records, including maps and letters.','One type of record only.','A single apple variety.','Various means several different kinds.'),Q('various.q2','various.s2','context','How many reasons did residents give?','More than one, across a range of reasons.','Exactly none.','Only one reason was given by everyone.','Various can mean more than one across a range.'),Q('various.q3','various.s1','distinction','Which collection is various?','A box containing coins, letters, and photographs.','A box of identical copies of one letter.','A box with a single photograph only.','The first contains different types of item.'),Q('various.q4','various.s2','grammar','Which sentence uses various before a plural noun?','Various neighbours offered to help.','Various neighbour offered to help.','A various of neighbours offered to help.','Various normally modifies a plural count noun.')]);
P('variously','From various + -ly, an adverb meaning in different ways, at different times, or under different names.',[C('variously.s1','不同方式或名称','The plant is variously known as sea lavender and marsh rosemary in coastal villages.','沿海村莊對這種植物有不同稱呼，例如海薰衣草和沼澤迷迭香。','be variously known / described / interpreted','Adverb: in various ways, at various times, or under various names.','Different communities use different names for the same plant.')],[M('The plant was variously known by one and only one name in every village and every source.','The plant was uniformly known by one name in every village and source.','One identical name everywhere is uniform, not various.')],[Q('variously.q1','variously.s1','meaning','How is the plant variously known?','It has different names in different coastal villages.','It has exactly one name everywhere.','It is never named.','Variously means under different names or in different ways.'),Q('variously.q2','variously.s1','context','Which account describes a tradition variously?','Sources explain it in several different ways.','Every source repeats the same wording.','No source mentions the tradition.','Different explanations are various ways of describing it.'),Q('variously.q3','variously.s1','grammar','What does variously modify in “The site is variously called…”?','The different names people use for the site.','The site’s colour.','The number of visitors.','The adverb describes differing ways of naming.'),Q('variously.q4','variously.s1','distinction','Which phrase fits variously?','variously described as a temple or a palace','described identically by every historian','described once with no alternate account','The first indicates different descriptions.')]);
P('varnish','From Old French vernis, from medieval Latin vernix; it is a clear coating and the act of covering a surface or concealing a fault.',[C('varnish.s1','透明涂层','A coat of varnish protected the wooden table from water and scratches.','一層清漆保護木桌，避免水漬和刮痕。','apply / coat / strip varnish','Noun: a transparent paint used to protect or decorate a surface; also the act of applying it.','The clear coating seals the wood.'),C('varnish.s1','掩饰缺陷','The report tried to varnish the delay with cheerful language instead of explaining its cause.','報告試圖用樂觀措辭掩飾延誤，沒有說明原因。','varnish over + flaw / truth','Verb: cover a surface or figuratively hide a fault with a glossy layer.','The wording glosses over the real problem.')],[M('The varnish left the table uncoated and exposed to water because it was never applied.','The bare table remained unvarnished and exposed to water.','If varnish is never applied, the table has no protective coating.')],[Q('varnish.q1','varnish.s1','meaning','What did the varnish do to the wooden table?','Protected it with a transparent coating.','Removed every layer from the wood.','Changed the table into a vase.','Varnish is a clear protective surface coating.'),Q('varnish.q2','varnish.s1','context','How did the report varnish the delay?','It covered the problem with cheerful wording instead of explaining it.','It applied clear paint to a table.','It gave a detailed account of the cause.','The verb can figuratively mean gloss over a fault.'),Q('varnish.q3','varnish.s1','distinction','Which use is literal?','A carpenter applies a clear finish to a cabinet.','A spokesperson glosses over a mistake.','A report hides a delay with pleasant language.','The carpenter applies an actual transparent coating.'),Q('varnish.q4','varnish.s1','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','She varnished over the budget error with vague praise.','He varnished the wooden railing to protect it.','They stripped old varnish from the chair.','The first hides a fault with polished language.')]);
P('varsity','Shortened from university; in North American usage it names a school or college’s principal sports team.',[C('varsity.s1','校队','Mina earned a place on the varsity basketball team after the final selection trial.','米娜通過最後選拔後，加入了校籃球隊。','the varsity team; play varsity sports','Noun: the principal sports team of a school, college, or university.','The team represents the institution at its main level.')],[M('Mina joined the varsity team by enrolling in an ordinary academic class with no sports team.','Mina joined the varsity team by earning a place on the school’s principal sports squad.','A varsity team is the institution’s main sports team, not an academic class.')],[Q('varsity.q1','varsity.s1','meaning','What did Mina earn a place on?','The school’s principal basketball team.','An ordinary academic class.','A theatre performance.','Varsity names a school or college’s main sports team.'),Q('varsity.q2','varsity.s1','context','Which student plays varsity?','A student selected for the university’s first team.','A student who watches games but is not selected.','A student taking a literature course.','Varsity status is membership on the main squad.'),Q('varsity.q3','varsity.s1','distinction','What does varsity distinguish?','The principal school team from other or junior teams.','A sports uniform from a school building.','A university from a city.','The term identifies the institution’s main team.'),Q('varsity.q4','varsity.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','She made the varsity volleyball squad.','She made the varsity classroom.','She made a varsity of old books.','Varsity modifies or names a principal sports team.')]);
P('varve','From Swedish varv, “layer or turn”; in geology a varve is an annual sediment layer.',[C('varve.s1','地质年层','The geologist counted each varve in the lake core to estimate how many years the sediments recorded.','地質學家計數湖泊岩芯中的每一道年層，以估算沉積物記錄了多少年。','count / measure a varve','Noun: an annual layer in lake or glacial sediment, used to count years.','Each deposited layer represents a year.')],[M('The geologist treated each varve as a daily cloud and counted thousands of them in one afternoon.','The geologist treated each varve as an annual sediment layer.','A varve is an annual sediment layer, not a cloud or daily event.')],[Q('varve.q1','varve.s1','meaning','What does each varve represent?','An annual layer in sediment.','A daily layer of clouds.','A type of sports team.','Varves can be counted to estimate years.'),Q('varve.q2','varve.s1','context','Why did the geologist count varves in the lake core?','To estimate the number of years recorded by the sediment.','To count plant varieties in a forest.','To measure the lake’s surface colour.','Each varve corresponds to a year.'),Q('varve.q3','varve.s1','distinction','Where might a geologist find varves?','In layered lake or glacial sediment.','In a basketball team roster.','On a polished wooden table.','Varves are annual sediment layers.'),Q('varve.q4','varve.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct geology phrase.','an annual varve in a lake-bed core','a varve in the school’s varsity lineup','a varve coating applied to a cabinet','A varve forms as a sediment layer.')]);
P('vary','From Latin variare, “change or make different”; it means be different or change something.',[C('vary.s1','随情况不同','The final delivery time may vary with traffic and weather conditions.','最終送達時間可能隨交通和天氣狀況而不同。','vary according to / with + factor','Intransitive verb: be different according to the situation.','Different conditions lead to different times.'),C('vary.s2','改变内容','The chef varies the soup each week by using vegetables that are in season.','廚師每週更換湯品內容，使用當季蔬菜。','vary + plan / menu / method','Transitive verb: change something so it is not always the same.','The chef deliberately changes the recipe.')],[M('Delivery times vary with weather, yet the service promises the exact same arrival minute in every storm.','Delivery times may change with weather, so the service does not promise the same arrival minute.','If a result varies with conditions, it is not identical in every circumstance.')],[Q('vary.q1','vary.s1','meaning','What may affect the delivery time?','Traffic and weather conditions.','The colour of the delivery van only.','The chef’s weekly menu.','The time differs according to conditions.'),Q('vary.q2','vary.s2','context','How does the chef vary the soup?','Changes the recipe using seasonal vegetables.','Serves the identical soup every week.','Measures the soup’s velocity.','This sense means deliberately change something.'),Q('vary.q3','vary.s1','distinction','Which statement uses vary intransitively?','Prices vary from shop to shop.','The chef varies the menu.','The editor varies the sentence.','The prices themselves differ.'),Q('vary.q4','vary.s2','grammar','Choose the transitive use.','The teacher varies the exercises each lesson.','The weather varies from day to day.','Delivery times vary with traffic.','The teacher acts on an object, the exercises.')]);
P('vascular','From Latin vascularis, “relating to vessels,” based on vasculum, “small vessel”; it applies to blood vessels or plant transport tissues.',[C('vascular.s1','血管或植物导管','The scan showed healthy vascular tissue around the patient’s repaired artery.','掃描顯示病人修復後的動脈周圍血管組織健康。','vascular system / tissue / plant','Adjective: relating to blood vessels in animals or xylem and phloem in plants.','The tissue is associated with vessels that transport fluid.')],[M('The vascular system carries blood through bones and muscles, but has no vessels.','The vascular system carries blood through blood vessels.','Vascular specifically relates to vessels that transport blood or plant fluids.')],[Q('vascular.q1','vascular.s1','meaning','What kind of tissue did the scan examine?','Tissue associated with blood vessels.','A theatre’s velvet curtain.','A lake sediment layer.','Vascular relates to vessels in the body.'),Q('vascular.q2','vascular.s1','context','Which plant structure is vascular?','Xylem and phloem that transport water and nutrients.','A flower petal’s colour only.','A root with no transport tissue.','The adjective also applies to plant conducting tissues.'),Q('vascular.q3','vascular.s1','distinction','Which topic is vascular medicine likely to study?','Blood vessels and circulation.','Annual layers in lake sediment.','A school’s sports team.','Vascular relates to the body’s vessels.'),Q('vascular.q4','vascular.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','vascular disease affecting the arteries','vascular varnish coating a table','vascular variation in a poem’s rhyme','Arteries are blood vessels, so the phrase is correct.')]);
P('vasculature','From vascular + -ature, naming the system or arrangement of vessels in a body or organ.',[C('vasculature.s1','血管网络','The MRI revealed an unusual vasculature supplying the tumour.','磁振造影顯示有一組異常血管網絡為腫瘤供血。','the vasculature of + organ / tissue','Noun: the system or pattern of vessels supplying a body or organ.','The vessels form a supply network.')],[M('The vasculature was a single empty room in the hospital, not a system of vessels.','The vascular system formed the blood-supply network around the tissue.','Vasculature names a vessel system, not a physical room.')],[Q('vasculature.q1','vasculature.s1','meaning','What did the MRI reveal?','A vessel network supplying the tumour.','A room with no blood vessels.','A range of flower colours.','Vasculature is the system or pattern of vessels.'),Q('vasculature.q2','vasculature.s1','context','What does the vasculature of an organ include?','The vessels that supply it.','Its decorative outer surface.','The body’s muscle strength.','The term names the organ’s vessel network.'),Q('vasculature.q3','vasculature.s1','distinction','Which finding concerns vasculature?','A map of arteries feeding a tissue.','A list of a team’s sports players.','A sediment layer in a lake.','Arteries form a vascular supply system.'),Q('vasculature.q4','vasculature.s1','word-choice','Choose the medical use.','the vasculature surrounding the organ','the velocity of the surgical tool','the variety of hospital curtains','The phrase describes vessels around an organ.')]);
P('vase','From French vase, from Latin vas, “vessel”; it is an open decorative container for flowers or display.',[C('vase.s1','花瓶或装饰器','The florist placed fresh tulips in a tall glass vase on the reception desk.','花藝師把新鮮鬱金香插在接待櫃檯上的高玻璃花瓶裡。','a vase for flowers; a decorative vase','Noun: an open decorative vessel used for flowers or as an ornament.','The container holds flowers and decorates the desk.')],[M('She arranged the tulips in a vase by putting them in an unopenable flat sheet of paper with no container.','She arranged the tulips in a vase, an open container made to hold flowers.','A vase is a vessel, not a flat sheet with no opening.')],[Q('vase.q1','vase.s1','meaning','What did the florist put the tulips in?','An open decorative container.','A sealed metal box.','A lake sediment core.','A vase is a vessel commonly used for flowers.'),Q('vase.q2','vase.s1','context','Which object is a vase?','A glass vessel holding a bouquet on a table.','A wall-mounted ventilation fan.','A velvet fabric square.','The glass vessel holds flowers.'),Q('vase.q3','vase.s1','distinction','What is the vase used for in the example?','Holding tulips while decorating the reception desk.','Measuring a river’s velocity.','Storing a school team roster.','It is a flower container and ornament.'),Q('vase.q4','vase.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','a vase filled with fresh flowers','a vase worn over the face','a vase carrying blood to the heart','A vase is an open decorative vessel for flowers.')]);
P('vast','From Latin vastus, “empty, immense”; it describes extreme size in area or amount.',[C('vast.s1','面积广阔','A vast plain stretched beyond the horizon, with no buildings in sight.','一片遼闊平原延伸到地平線之外，看不見任何建築。','a vast area / landscape / plain','Adjective: extremely large in area.','The plain extends over a huge space.'),C('vast.s2','数量程度巨大','The project required a vast amount of data from hospitals across the country.','這項計畫需要來自全國各地醫院的大量資料。','a vast number / amount / cost','Adjective: extremely great in number, cost, or degree.','The quantity of data is enormous.')],[M('The vast plain was a tiny patch of land smaller than a garden plot.','The small plain was a tiny patch of land smaller than a garden plot.','A tiny area is not vast in physical extent.')],[Q('vast.q1','vast.s1','meaning','How large was the plain?','It extended over an enormous area beyond the horizon.','It was smaller than a garden.','It was a single room.','Vast can describe extreme area.'),Q('vast.q2','vast.s2','context','What did the project require?','An extremely large amount of data.','A few figures from one clinic.','A single vase.','Vast can describe a great quantity.'),Q('vast.q3','vast.s1','distinction','Which landscape is vast?','A desert extending hundreds of kilometres.','A small courtyard behind one house.','A narrow shelf.','The desert covers an immense area.'),Q('vast.q4','vast.s2','word-choice','Choose the use meaning “very great in number.”','a vast number of survey responses','a vast plain across the country','a vast open landscape','The first describes a huge quantity.')]);
P('vastly','From vast + -ly, an adverb meaning by a very large amount or extent.',[C('vastly.s1','大幅度','The new pump is vastly more efficient than the damaged model it replaced.','新水泵比被替換的受損型號效率高得多。','vastly + comparative adjective','Adverb: by a very large amount or extent.','The difference in efficiency is substantial.')],[M('The new pump is vastly more efficient, but its measured output differs from the old one by only one drop a year.','The new pump is slightly more efficient, with only a tiny difference in annual output.','A difference of one drop a year is slight, not vast.')],[Q('vastly.q1','vastly.s1','meaning','How does the new pump compare?','It is more efficient by a large amount.','It is only one drop more efficient a year.','It is exactly identical in every measure.','Vastly means by a very large extent.'),Q('vastly.q2','vastly.s1','context','Which result improved vastly?','The team reduced waiting time from ten hours to ten minutes.','The team reduced it from ten hours to nine hours and fifty-nine minutes.','The time remained exactly the same.','A dramatic reduction is a very large change.'),Q('vastly.q3','vastly.s1','grammar','What does vastly modify in “vastly different”?','The degree of difference.','The noun pump.','The location of the pump.','The adverb intensifies the adjective different.'),Q('vastly.q4','vastly.s1','distinction','Choose the phrase that fits a major improvement.','vastly better results after replacing the pump','vastly identical copies with no change','vastly a result that stayed the same','The results improved by a large amount.')]);
P('vastness','From vast + -ness, the quality of being immense in size or extent.',[C('vastness.s1','辽阔程度','The vastness of the desert became clear when the hikers saw no road or settlement for days.','健行者數日看不到道路或聚落後，才真正感受到沙漠的遼闊。','the vastness of + area / space','Noun: immense size or extent.','The desert covers an enormous region.')],[M('The vastness of the desert was obvious because it covered only a few square metres.','The small size of the desert was obvious because it covered only a few square metres.','A few square metres is small, not immense in extent.')],[Q('vastness.q1','vastness.s1','meaning','What became clear to the hikers?','The desert’s immense size and extent.','The desert covered only a few square metres.','A city’s population.','Vastness names immense size.'),Q('vastness.q2','vastness.s1','context','Which scene suggests vastness?','An ocean stretching beyond every visible horizon.','A small pond inside a courtyard.','A single cup on a desk.','The ocean extends across a huge area.'),Q('vastness.q3','vastness.s1','distinction','Which noun names the quality of being vast?','vastness','variety','velocity','Vastness is the immense size or extent.'),Q('vastness.q4','vastness.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','the vastness of the open plain','the vastness of a tiny stamp','the vastness of one grain of sand','The open plain has immense extent.')]);
P('vaudeville','From French vaudeville, a popular variety-theatre form especially in the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries.',[C('vaudeville.s1','剧场表演','The museum’s archive preserves posters from a vaudeville theatre that featured comic sketches and songs.','博物館檔案保存著一間雜耍劇場的海報，當年節目包括喜劇短劇和歌曲。','a vaudeville show / theatre','Noun: popular variety theatre of the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries.','The programme combines different kinds of stage acts.')],[M('The vaudeville show consisted of a single silent lecture with no variety acts or entertainment.','The lecture was not a vaudeville show because it had no variety of stage acts.','Vaudeville is a variety-theatre form, not simply a single lecture.')],[Q('vaudeville.q1','vaudeville.s1','meaning','What kind of theatre was vaudeville?','Popular variety theatre with different stage acts.','A silent scientific lecture only.','A school sports team.','Vaudeville presented a variety of performances.'),Q('vaudeville.q2','vaudeville.s1','context','What might a vaudeville programme include?','Comic sketches, songs, and other short acts.','One long courtroom verdict.','A geology report on sediment.','The form featured varied entertainment acts.'),Q('vaudeville.q3','vaudeville.s1','distinction','When was vaudeville especially popular?','The late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries.','Only in ancient Rome.','Only in the present decade.','The dictionary sense specifies that historical period.'),Q('vaudeville.q4','vaudeville.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate description.','a poster advertising a vaudeville variety show','a notice for a single school lecture','a chart measuring vessel pressure','Vaudeville is a popular variety-theatre form.')]);
P('vault','From Old French volte, “arched roof,” from Latin volvere, “turn”; it names an arch, a secure room, or a leap over something.',[C('vault.s1','拱顶','The stone vault above the chapel rested on thick columns.','小教堂上方的石砌拱頂由厚重柱子支撐。','a stone / barrel vault','Noun: an arched roof or ceiling, especially one made of stone.','The ceiling curves into an arch.'),C('vault.s2','金库','The bank stored rare documents in a climate-controlled vault.','銀行把珍貴文件存放在恆溫金庫裡。','a bank / document vault','Noun: a strong secure room where valuables are kept.','The room protects valuable items.'),C('vault.s3','跳跃','The athlete used both hands to vault over the low barrier.','運動員用雙手支撐，躍過低矮障礙。','vault over + obstacle','Verb: jump over something using a pole or one’s hands.','The athlete clears the barrier with a leap.')],[M('The athlete vaulted over the barrier by remaining on the ground and walking around it.','The athlete walked around the barrier instead of vaulting over it.','Walking around does not involve jumping over the obstacle.')],[Q('vault.q1','vault.s1','meaning','What shape was the chapel ceiling?','An arch supported by columns.','A flat sheet of wood.','A secure bank room.','A vault can be an arched roof or ceiling.'),Q('vault.q2','vault.s2','context','Where did the bank store rare documents?','In a secure, climate-controlled room.','On the chapel’s stone roof.','On an athlete’s pole.','A vault is a strong room for valuables.'),Q('vault.q3','vault.s3','distinction','How did the athlete clear the barrier?','Jumped over it using both hands for support.','Walked around it on the ground.','Stored it in a bank.','To vault is to leap over an obstacle.'),Q('vault.q4','vault.s1','word-choice','Choose the architectural use.','a vaulted chamber with a curved stone ceiling','a bank vault for keeping jewellery','a gymnast vaulting over a horse','The chamber has an arched ceiling.')]);
P('vaulted','From vault + -ed, describing a ceiling built with a curved arch.',[C('vaulted.s1','拱形天花板','The vaulted hall echoed as the choir sang beneath its high stone ceiling.','合唱團在高聳石砌拱頂下歌唱，聲音在大廳裡迴盪。','a vaulted ceiling / hall','Adjective: built with a vault, so the ceiling curves like an arch.','The roof forms a high curved arch.')],[M('The hall had a vaulted ceiling that was perfectly flat from wall to wall with no curve.','The hall had a flat ceiling with no vault or arch.','A vaulted ceiling curves into an arch rather than remaining flat.')],[Q('vaulted.q1','vaulted.s1','meaning','What was the hall’s ceiling like?','High and curved like an arch.','Flat with no curve.','A secure room for valuables.','Vaulted describes an arched ceiling.'),Q('vaulted.q2','vaulted.s1','context','Why did the choir’s sound echo?','It sang beneath a high vaulted stone ceiling.','It sang in an open field.','The singers were inside a bank vault.','The architecture includes a high curved roof.'),Q('vaulted.q3','vaulted.s1','distinction','Which room is vaulted?','A hall with a curved brick ceiling.','A room with a flat plaster ceiling.','A secure underground room with a locked door but flat roof.','The curved ceiling is a vault.'),Q('vaulted.q4','vaulted.s1','word-choice','Choose the architectural phrase.','a vaulted stone roof over the chapel','a vault used to store cash','an athlete who vaults over a bar','Vaulted describes the roof’s arched construction.')]);
P('vector','From Latin vector, “carrier,” from vehere, “carry”; in mathematics it is directed, and in medicine or genetics it carries an agent or DNA.',[C('vector.s1','数学或生物','The researcher used a viral vector to carry a harmless gene into the test cells.','研究人員使用病毒載體，將無害基因帶入測試細胞。','a vector carries / represents + something','Noun: a directed mathematical quantity, a pathogen carrier, or a carrier used to insert DNA.','The vector transports genetic material into cells.')],[M('The wind-speed vector had no direction, magnitude, or role in the calculation.','The scalar wind speed had no direction, while a vector includes direction and magnitude.','A vector is directed; an amount without direction is a scalar.')],[Q('vector.q1','vector.s1','meaning','What did the viral vector carry into the test cells?','A harmless gene.','A vase.','A verdict.','In biology, a vector can carry DNA into a cell.'),Q('vector.q2','vector.s1','context','What distinguishes a mathematical vector from an ordinary scalar?','It includes direction as well as magnitude.','It contains no numerical amount.','It is always a virus.','A vector is a directed quantity.'),Q('vector.q3','vector.s1','distinction','Which organism could be a disease vector?','A mosquito carrying a pathogen between hosts.','A leaf vein carrying water.','A car transporting passengers.','A pathogen vector transmits an infectious agent.'),Q('vector.q4','vector.s1','word-choice','Choose the genetic-engineering use.','A vector delivered the DNA sequence into the cells.','The vector showed the direction of the wind on a chart.','A vector moved the injured passenger to hospital.','The first is a carrier used to insert DNA.')]);
P('veer','From Old English fēr, “turn aside,” from the movement of a ship or wind; it means change direction, opinion, or course.',[C('veer.s1','转向或改变路线','The cyclist veered left to avoid a fallen branch in the road.','騎士為了避開路上的斷枝而向左轉。','veer left / away from / toward','Intransitive verb: turn aside from a course, opinion, or wind direction.','The cyclist changes direction to avoid an obstacle.')],[M('The cyclist veered left by continuing perfectly straight down the middle of the road.','The cyclist stayed on course by continuing straight down the middle of the road.','Veering means turning aside, not continuing straight.')],[Q('veer.q1','veer.s1','meaning','Why did the cyclist veer left?','To avoid a fallen branch.','To ride straight into the branch.','To repair the road.','Veer means turn aside from a course.'),Q('veer.q2','veer.s1','context','What happened when the wind veered north?','Its direction changed toward the north.','It stopped being air.','It became a mathematical scalar.','The verb applies to a change in wind direction.'),Q('veer.q3','veer.s1','distinction','Which speaker veers from the topic?','A speaker turns to an unrelated issue mid-discussion.','A speaker continues the same argument.','A speaker ends the meeting.','The speaker changes course in the discussion.'),Q('veer.q4','veer.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural road use.','The car veered away from the roadblock.','The car veered by staying on the exact same line.','The car veered into a parked position without moving.','The car turns aside to avoid the obstacle.')]);
P('vegetable','From Latin vegetabilis, “animating or enlivening”; it names an edible plant and can describe plant-derived material.',[C('vegetable.s1','可食植物','Roasted vegetable dishes accompanied the rice, including carrots, squash, and leafy greens.','烤蔬菜料理搭配米飯上桌，包括紅蘿蔔、南瓜和葉菜。','a vegetable; vegetable + dish / garden','Noun: a plant grown for food, usually eaten with a meal and not counted as a fruit.' ,'The examples are edible plants served with the meal.'),C('vegetable.s2','植物性的','The label says the soap contains vegetable oils rather than animal fat.','標籤說明這款肥皂含植物油，而非動物脂肪。','vegetable + oil / matter','Adjective: coming from plants rather than animals.','The oils are plant-derived.')],[M('The cook served a vegetable dish made entirely from beef and fish.','The cook served an animal-based dish made from beef and fish.','Beef and fish come from animals, not vegetables.')],[Q('vegetable.q1','vegetable.s1','meaning','Which foods were served as vegetables?','Carrots, squash, and leafy greens.','Beef and fish.','Soap and plant oils.','Vegetables are edible plants served with food.'),Q('vegetable.q2','vegetable.s2','context','What does “vegetable oils” mean on the soap label?','Oils that come from plants.','Oils extracted from fish.','Oils made from glass.','Vegetable as an adjective means plant-derived.'),Q('vegetable.q3','vegetable.s1','distinction','Which item is a vegetable in the meal sense?','A carrot roasted and served with rice.','A bottle of plant-based soap.','A fish caught in the river.','The carrot is an edible plant served as food.'),Q('vegetable.q4','vegetable.s2','word-choice','Choose the plant-origin adjective use.','vegetable shortening made from plant oils','a vegetable garden growing carrots','a vegetable dish served for lunch','The shortening is made from plant material.')]);
P('vegetarian','From vegetable + -arian; it describes a person who avoids meat and fish or food made without them.',[C('vegetarian.s1','饮食者','As a vegetarian, Dinesh ordered the lentil curry and checked that the broth contained no fish.','身為素食者，迪內希點了扁豆咖哩，並確認湯底不含魚。','a vegetarian; follow a vegetarian diet','Noun: a person who does not eat meat or fish.','He chooses a meal without animal flesh.'),C('vegetarian.s2','食物','The café added a vegetarian pie filled with mushrooms, spinach, and cheese.','咖啡館新增了一款以蘑菇、菠菜和起司為餡的素食派。','a vegetarian meal / dish / option','Adjective: made without meat or fish.','The pie contains no meat or fish.')],[M('The vegetarian ordered a beef steak because he followed a diet that excludes no meat or fish.','The meat-eater ordered a beef steak because he followed a diet that includes meat.','Someone who eats beef does not follow the vegetarian diet described here.')],[Q('vegetarian.q1','vegetarian.s1','meaning','Why did Dinesh check the curry broth?','He avoids meat and fish as a vegetarian.','He wanted a beef stock.','He was checking whether it contained vegetables only.','A vegetarian does not eat meat or fish.'),Q('vegetarian.q2','vegetarian.s2','context','What makes the mushroom pie vegetarian?','It is made without meat or fish.','It contains beef and fish.','It is a person who avoids meat.','Vegetarian as an adjective describes food without meat or fish.'),Q('vegetarian.q3','vegetarian.s1','distinction','Which person is vegetarian by this definition?','Someone who eats lentils but avoids meat and fish.','Someone who eats fish but avoids beef.','Someone who eats chicken daily.','Vegetarians avoid both meat and fish.'),Q('vegetarian.q4','vegetarian.s2','word-choice','Choose the food use.','a vegetarian soup made with beans and vegetables','a vegetarian who orders fish','a vegetarian person avoiding all cooking','The soup is made without meat or fish.')]);
P('vegetation','From Latin vegetatio, “growth or animation,” based on vegetare, “grow”; it means plants in a place, plant growth, or, in older literary use, dull inactivity.',[C('vegetation.s1','植物群','Dense vegetation covered the riverbank, including reeds, shrubs, and young trees.','河岸被茂密植被覆蓋，包括蘆葦、灌木和幼樹。','vegetation in / along + place','Noun: all the plants growing in a particular place.','The plants form the riverbank cover.'),C('vegetation.s2','生长或迟钝状态','After the illness, the old novel describes his life as mere vegetation, with little activity or awareness.','那部舊小說把他病後的生活形容為單調遲鈍、缺乏活動與意識的狀態。','vegetation of plants; literary “mere vegetation”','Noun: plant growth; in old literary use, a dull inactive life.','The dated figurative use means passive inactivity.')],[M('Dense vegetation covered the riverbank, but the bank had no plants growing anywhere.','Bare ground covered the riverbank, with no vegetation growing there.','Vegetation means plant life; bare ground without plants is not vegetation.')],[Q('vegetation.q1','vegetation.s1','meaning','What covered the riverbank?','Reeds, shrubs, and young trees.','A paved road with no plants.','A single garden tool.','Vegetation is all the plants growing in an area.'),Q('vegetation.q2','vegetation.s2','context','What does the old novel mean by “mere vegetation”?','A dull, inactive life with little awareness.','Dense shrubs along a riverbank.','An energetic life full of varied activity.','This is an older figurative sense of passive inactivity.'),Q('vegetation.q3','vegetation.s1','distinction','Which report concerns plant cover?','Vegetation along the stream was thick after the rainy season.','The patient lived in a state of mere vegetation.','The river level varied after rain.','The first describes plants growing in a place.'),Q('vegetation.q4','vegetation.s2','word-choice','Choose the older figurative use.','The critic called his passive routine a kind of vegetation.','The botanist surveyed vegetation in the marsh.','Vegetation filled the slope with wildflowers.','The first uses the literary sense of dull inactivity.')]);
P('vegetative','From vegetate + -ive; it relates to plant growth, seedless reproduction, or basic bodily function without consciousness.',[C('vegetative.s1','植物生长','The vegetative growth of the fern produced broad leaves before it formed spores.','蕨類先進行營養生長，長出大片葉片，之後才形成孢子。','vegetative growth / stage','Adjective: relating to plant growth rather than reproduction.' ,'The fern is growing leaves, not reproducing.'),C('vegetative.s2','无性繁殖','Strawberry plants can spread by vegetative reproduction through runners that root in the soil.','草莓可透過匍匐莖扎根進行營養繁殖。','vegetative reproduction; vegetative propagation','Adjective: producing new plants without seeds, as from stems or roots.','The new plant grows from a runner rather than a seed.'),C('vegetative.s3','基本生理功能','The doctor explained that the patient remained in a vegetative state with basic body functions but no conscious thought.','醫師說明病人仍處於植物狀態，保有基本身體功能但沒有意識思考。','a vegetative state','Adjective: showing basic body functions without conscious thought.','This is a serious medical description of the patient’s condition.')],[M('The fern’s vegetative reproduction began when it produced seeds rather than runners or roots.','The fern reproduced by seeds rather than vegetatively through runners or roots.','Vegetative reproduction produces plants without seeds, such as from runners.')],[Q('vegetative.q1','vegetative.s1','meaning','What did the fern produce during vegetative growth?','Broad leaves before forming spores.','Seeds before any leaves appeared.','A new plant from a runner.','This sense concerns plant growth rather than reproduction.'),Q('vegetative.q2','vegetative.s2','context','How did the strawberries reproduce vegetatively?','Runners rooted in the soil and formed new plants.','Seeds were planted in a greenhouse.','Leaves stopped growing.','Vegetative reproduction can occur from stems or roots.'),Q('vegetative.q3','vegetative.s3','distinction','What does vegetative state mean in the doctor’s explanation?','Basic body functions continue without conscious thought.','The patient is growing plant leaves.','The patient is reproducing without seeds.','The medical sense refers to limited bodily function without awareness.'),Q('vegetative.q4','vegetative.s2','word-choice','Choose the plant-propagation use.','New strawberry plants formed from rooting runners.','The fern grew leaves before making spores.','The doctor described a patient’s state of consciousness.','Runners produce plants without seeds.')]);
P('vehemence','From Latin vehementia, “violence or force,” based on vehemens, “impetuous”; it is strong passionate or angry force in speech and action.',[C('vehemence.s1','强烈情感','She argued with such vehemence that the committee paused to hear her evidence.','她以強烈激昂的語氣陳述，委員會因此停下來聽她的證據。','speak / argue with vehemence','Noun: strong and passionate feeling shown in words or actions.','Her emotion is forceful and visible.'),C('vehemence.s2','愤怒抗议','The residents expressed their vehemence against the unfair eviction notice.','居民強烈憤怒地抗議不公平的驅逐通知。','vehemence against + injustice / policy','Noun: angry force in speech against something unfair.','Their anger is directed at an unjust action.')],[M('She spoke with vehemence, but her calm whisper showed no passion, force, or emotion.','She spoke calmly and without vehemence.','A calm whisper without passion is the opposite of vehemence.')],[Q('vehemence.q1','vehemence.s1','meaning','How did she argue before the committee?','With strong, passionate force.','In a calm whisper without emotion.','By silently leaving the room.','Vehemence is intense feeling shown in words or actions.'),Q('vehemence.q2','vehemence.s2','context','Why were residents speaking with vehemence?','They were angrily protesting an unfair eviction.','They were thanking the landlord for fair treatment.','They were discussing a plant’s growth.','This sense is angry force against an injustice.'),Q('vehemence.q3','vehemence.s1','distinction','Which speaker shows vehemence?','A speaker passionately defends the endangered clinic.','A speaker reads a neutral list in a flat voice.','A speaker says nothing.','The first shows strong emotion.'),Q('vehemence.q4','vehemence.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about angry opposition.','the vehemence of the protest against the unfair rule','the calmness of a quiet conversation','the velocity of a moving vehicle','Vehemence describes the protest’s angry force.')]);
P('vehement','From Latin vehemens, “forceful or impetuous”; it describes strong criticism, feeling, or physical force.',[C('vehement.s1','强烈反对','The committee issued a vehement objection to removing the village clinic.','委員會強烈反對拆除村裡的診所。','a vehement objection / criticism','Adjective: expressing strong and forceful criticism or opposition.','The objection is emphatic and forceful.'),C('vehement.s2','热情支持','Fans gave a vehement welcome to the returning captain after the final match.','決賽後，球迷熱烈歡迎歸隊的隊長。','vehement support / enthusiasm','Adjective: showing very strong and passionate feeling or support.','Their welcome expresses intense positive feeling.'),C('vehement.s3','猛烈力量','A vehement gust slammed the gate shut during the storm.','暴風雨中，一陣猛烈的強風吹得大門砰然關上。','a vehement force / gust','Adjective: acting with great physical force or violence.','The gust has powerful physical force.')],[M('The committee gave a vehement objection by quietly agreeing with every proposal and expressing no opposition.','The committee gave a mild objection by quietly expressing a small concern.','Quiet agreement with no opposition is not a vehement objection.')],[Q('vehement.q1','vehement.s1','meaning','What was the committee’s response to removing the clinic?','A forceful objection.','Quiet agreement.','A warm welcome to the captain.','Vehement criticism or opposition is strongly expressed.'),Q('vehement.q2','vehement.s2','context','How did fans welcome the captain?','With intensely passionate support.','With no emotion or applause.','With a physical gust of wind.','Vehement can describe strong positive feeling.'),Q('vehement.q3','vehement.s3','distinction','What did the storm’s vehement gust do?','Slammed the gate shut with force.','Expressed an opinion about the clinic.','Welcomed a sports captain.','This sense refers to powerful physical action.'),Q('vehement.q4','vehement.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase showing strong opposition.','a vehement protest against the closure','a mild question about the schedule','a warm welcome after a match','The protest is forceful criticism.')]);
P('vehicle','From Latin vehiculum, “means of transport,” based on vehere, “carry”; it can transport people or carry an idea.',[C('vehicle.s1','交通工具','The electric vehicle carried the survey team across the rough farm road.','電動車載著勘查隊穿越崎嶇的農路。','a vehicle for transport','Noun: a car, bus, lorry, or similar machine for land transport.','The machine carries people along a road.'),C('vehicle.s2','表达或实现媒介','The documentary became a vehicle for discussing water access in remote communities.','這部紀錄片成為討論偏遠社區用水問題的媒介。','a vehicle for + idea / aim','Noun: something used to express an idea or achieve an aim.','The film carries the discussion to an audience.')],[M('The documentary was a vehicle for the debate, but it transported viewers physically along a road in a bus.','The bus was the vehicle that transported viewers along the road to the debate.','A documentary can carry ideas, but the bus is the physical transport vehicle.')],[Q('vehicle.q1','vehicle.s1','meaning','What carried the survey team on the farm road?','An electric road machine.','A documentary.','A plant vessel.','A vehicle is a machine for land transport.'),Q('vehicle.q2','vehicle.s2','context','How did the documentary function?','It provided a way to discuss water access.','It physically carried viewers along a road.','It measured plant growth.','A vehicle can be a means for expressing an idea.'),Q('vehicle.q3','vehicle.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses vehicle literally?','The bus is the vehicle for the school trip.','The novel became a vehicle for social criticism.','Music can be a vehicle for emotion.','The bus is a transport machine.'),Q('vehicle.q4','vehicle.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','The poem served as a vehicle for the writer’s grief.','The van served as a vehicle for delivery.','The car carried the team to the site.','The poem communicates an idea or feeling.')]);
P('vehicles','Plural of vehicle; it means road transport machines or, figuratively, several means of expressing or achieving something.',[C('vehicles.s1','道路交通','Vehicles slowed to a crawl as road crews cleared stones from the mountain pass.','道路工人清除山口石塊時，車輛只能緩慢前行。','vehicles on / in traffic','Plural noun: road vehicles considered together, especially in traffic.','Cars and trucks form a group in traffic.'),C('vehicles.s2','表达媒介','The artists used songs and short films as vehicles for their campaign message.','藝術家用歌曲和短片作為傳達活動訴求的媒介。','vehicles for + message / change','Plural noun: means of expressing or achieving something.','The works carry a message to the public.')],[M('Vehicles slowed in traffic, but the road was entirely empty and contained no cars or trucks.','Traffic flowed freely because the road was empty of vehicles.','An empty road has no vehicles to slow down.')],[Q('vehicles.q1','vehicles.s1','meaning','Why did vehicles slow at the pass?','Crews were clearing stones from the road.','The artists were screening a film.','No road users were present.','Vehicles in this sense are road transport machines.'),Q('vehicles.q2','vehicles.s2','context','How did artists use songs and films?','As means to communicate their campaign message.','As road machines to clear stones.','As a traffic jam.','A vehicle can be a means of expression.'),Q('vehicles.q3','vehicles.s1','distinction','Which scene contains vehicles?','Cars and lorries queue on a busy bridge.','A poem expresses an idea.','A song carries a campaign message.','The queue is a group of road machines.'),Q('vehicles.q4','vehicles.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative plural.','Stories became vehicles for the community’s history.','Vehicles crossed the bridge in heavy traffic.','The truck was a vehicle for farm tools.','Stories carry and express a message.')]);
P('veil','From Old French voile, from Latin velum, “covering”; it can be cloth, a concealment, or the act of hiding.',[C('veil.s1','面纱','The bride lifted her veil before exchanging rings with her partner.','新娘在交換戒指前掀起面紗。','wear / lift / remove a veil','Noun: thin cloth worn over the head and often the face.','The cloth covers part of the face.'),C('veil.s2','掩盖物','A veil of secrecy surrounded the negotiations until the agreement was signed.','協議簽署前，談判一直籠罩在保密之中。','a veil of + secrecy / mist / uncertainty','Noun: something that hides a fact or feeling.','Secrecy conceals the details.'),C('veil.s3','遮掩','He tried to veil his disappointment with a quick smile.','他試圖用一抹迅速的微笑掩飾失望。','veil + feeling / intention','Verb: cover something or hide a feeling.','The smile masks his true emotion.')],[M('He veiled his disappointment by announcing it loudly to everyone and making no attempt to hide it.','He expressed his disappointment openly and made no attempt to veil it.','Making a feeling public does not veil or hide it.')],[Q('veil.q1','veil.s1','meaning','What did the bride lift?','A thin cloth worn over her head or face.','A bank’s secure room.','A leaf’s blood vessel.','A veil can be cloth worn over the head or face.'),Q('veil.q2','veil.s2','context','What surrounded the negotiations?','Secrecy that concealed the details.','A clear public announcement.','A wedding garment.','A figurative veil can hide facts.'),Q('veil.q3','veil.s3','distinction','How did he try to veil his disappointment?','By hiding it behind a quick smile.','By announcing it openly.','By wearing a sports uniform.','The verb means conceal a feeling.'),Q('veil.q4','veil.s1','word-choice','Choose the literal use.','a sheer veil covering the bride’s face','a veil of secrecy over talks','to veil his disappointment','The first is an actual piece of cloth.')]);
P('vein','From Old French veine, from Latin vena; it names a blood vessel, a line or ore layer, or a characteristic style.',[C('vein.s1','血管','The nurse found a vein in the patient’s arm before taking a blood sample.','護理師採血前，在病人手臂上找到一條靜脈。','a vein in + body part','Noun: a tube carrying blood from body parts back toward the heart.','The vessel returns blood toward the heart.'),C('vein.s2','纹路或矿脉','Thin white veins ran through the dark marble used for the counter.','櫃檯用的深色大理石中穿著細白紋路。','veins in + leaf / rock / wood','Noun: a thin line in a leaf, rock, or wood; also a layer of ore.','The white lines pattern the stone.'),C('vein.s3','风格或情绪','The second chapter continues in a comic vein after the serious opening.','第二章在嚴肅的開頭後，延續了滑稽的風格。','in a + adjective + vein','Noun: a particular style, mood, or quality.','The chapter’s style is comic.')],[M('The nurse found a vein in the patient’s arm, but the arm contained no blood vessels at all.','The nurse found a vein in the patient’s arm, one of the vessels carrying blood toward the heart.','A vein is itself a blood vessel.')],[Q('vein.q1','vein.s1','meaning','What did the nurse locate in the arm?','A blood vessel for drawing a sample.','A marble pattern.','A comic writing style.','A vein carries blood toward the heart.'),Q('vein.q2','vein.s2','context','What were the white lines in the marble?','Veins running through the stone.','Blood vessels in the counter.','A comic chapter.','A vein can be a line or layer in rock.'),Q('vein.q3','vein.s3','distinction','What does “in a comic vein” describe?','The style or mood of the writing.','A blood vessel in a performer.','The marble’s white pattern.','Vein can mean a characteristic style.'),Q('vein.q4','vein.s1','word-choice','Choose the medical use.','A vein carries blood back toward the heart.','The poem continues in a humorous vein.','White veins pattern the marble slab.','The first is a blood vessel.')]);
P('veining','From vein + -ing, naming lines resembling veins in stone, leaves, or wings.',[C('veining.s1','纹理','The delicate veining in the marble formed pale branches across its dark surface.','大理石細緻的脈紋在深色表面形成淡色枝狀線條。','veining in + marble / leaf / wing','Noun: lines like veins in marble, a leaf, or an insect wing.','The pale lines resemble branching veins.')],[M('The marble’s veining formed no lines or patterns at all and left the stone completely uniform.','The marble was un-veined and completely uniform, with no lines or patterns.','Veining refers to visible lines or patterns in the material.')],[Q('veining.q1','veining.s1','meaning','What pattern appeared in the marble?','Pale branching lines across the dark stone.','A perfectly uniform surface with no marks.','A blood sample in a tube.','Veining names vein-like lines in a material.'),Q('veining.q2','veining.s1','context','Which leaf feature is its veining?','The branching lines that carry fluids through the leaf.','The leaf’s smooth waxy surface only.','The stem’s flower colour.','The lines resemble a network of veins.'),Q('veining.q3','veining.s1','distinction','Which object might show veining?','A butterfly wing with fine branching lines.','A flat sheet with no pattern.','A glass vase with a clear surface only.','Veining can describe lines in an insect wing.'),Q('veining.q4','veining.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','the green veining of the leaf','the veining of a plain surface with no lines','the veining of the school team roster','Veining refers to vein-like lines in a surface.')]);
P('velocity','From Latin velocitas, “swiftness,” based on velox, “swift”; in physics it includes direction, and formally it can mean great speed.',[C('velocity.s1','物理速度','The probe’s velocity increased eastward as it moved farther from the planet.','探測器離行星越遠，向東的速度越快。','velocity in a direction; change in velocity','Noun: the rate at which something moves in a particular direction.','Both speed and direction matter.'),C('velocity.s2','高速','The cyclist descended the hill at considerable velocity.','騎士以相當快的速度下山。','at high / considerable velocity','Noun: great speed, especially in formal writing.','The cyclist is moving quickly.')],[M('The probe’s velocity was a direction with no rate of movement or speed.','The probe’s velocity described its speed and direction of movement.','Velocity includes a rate of movement along a direction.')],[Q('velocity.q1','velocity.s1','meaning','What information did the probe’s velocity include?','Its rate of movement eastward.','Only its colour.','Only its distance from the planet.','Velocity specifies movement in a particular direction.'),Q('velocity.q2','velocity.s2','context','How fast did the cyclist descend?','At considerable speed.','At a complete stop.','At a rate with no movement.','Velocity can mean great speed in formal use.'),Q('velocity.q3','velocity.s1','distinction','How is velocity different from speed in physics?','Velocity includes direction.','Velocity has no magnitude.','Velocity applies only to plants.','The directional information distinguishes velocity.'),Q('velocity.q4','velocity.s2','word-choice','Choose the formal use meaning speed.','The object struck the barrier at high velocity.','The eastward velocity changed direction.','The vector showed direction and magnitude.','The phrase means the object was moving very fast.')]);
P('velvet','From Old French veluotte, diminutive of velu, “hairy”; it names a soft piled cloth and things made or soft like it.',[C('velvet.s1','布料','She chose dark velvet for the theatre curtain because its thick pile absorbed light.','她選用深色天鵝絨做劇院窗簾，因為厚絨毛能吸光。','velvet fabric / dress / curtain','Noun: cloth with a soft, thick surface of short upright threads.','The fabric’s pile feels soft and dense.'),C('velvet.s2','天鹅绒制或柔软','The velvet lining kept the delicate instrument from sliding inside its case.','天鵝絨襯裡讓精密儀器不會在盒內滑動。','velvet + lining / touch; feel like velvet','Adjective: made of velvet or soft in the same way.','The lining has a velvet-like texture.')],[M('The velvet curtain had a rough surface of long sharp wires that scratched every hand.','The wire curtain had a rough surface that scratched every hand.','Velvet has a soft pile, not a sharp wire surface.')],[Q('velvet.q1','velvet.s1','meaning','Why did the theatre choose velvet curtains?','The thick soft pile absorbed light.','The cloth was made of sharp wires.','The fabric was a school sports team.','Velvet is a soft cloth with short upright threads.'),Q('velvet.q2','velvet.s2','context','What did the velvet lining do in the instrument case?','Its soft texture kept the instrument from sliding.','It measured the instrument’s velocity.','It carried blood back to the heart.','The adjective describes material or a similar softness.'),Q('velvet.q3','velvet.s1','distinction','Which item is velvet fabric?','A short-pile cloth used for a curtain.','A glass container for flowers.','A stone ceiling arch.','Velvet is a kind of soft piled cloth.'),Q('velvet.q4','velvet.s2','word-choice','Choose the adjective use.','a velvet touch on the padded case','a length of velvet cloth by the window','a roll of velvet sold by the metre','The first describes a soft, velvet-like quality.')]);
P('vend','From Latin vendere, “sell,” a formal verb for selling goods or property.',[C('vend.s1','出售','The cooperative will vend fresh fruit and bread at the station market each morning.','合作社每天早晨會在車站市集販售新鮮水果和麵包。','vend goods / property','Transitive verb: sell goods or property, in formal language.','The cooperative offers products for sale.')],[M('The cooperative vended the fruit by giving every item away and accepting no payment.','The cooperative gave the fruit away instead of vending it.','Vend means sell; freely giving goods away is not vending.')],[Q('vend.q1','vend.s1','meaning','What will the cooperative do at the market?','Sell fruit and bread.','Give away all goods for free.','Repair the station roof.','Vend is a formal verb meaning sell.'),Q('vend.q2','vend.s1','context','Which action is vending?','Offering bottled water for sale from a stand.','Donating water without payment.','Drinking water at home.','The stand sells goods.'),Q('vend.q3','vend.s1','distinction','What register does vend have?','Formal.','Only slang.','A term for gardening.','Vend is a formal word for selling.'),Q('vend.q4','vend.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct use.','The firm vended the property to a local buyer.','The firm vend the property yesterday.','The firm vended the property by refusing to sell it.','Vended means sold the property.')]);
P('vendor','From Latin vendere, “sell,” through Anglo-French; it means a seller in a market or the person or firm selling property or a service.',[C('vendor.s1','摊贩','A street vendor sold roasted chestnuts outside the station on winter evenings.','冬夜裡，街頭小販在車站外販售烤栗子。','a street / market vendor','Noun: a person who sells food or small goods in a street or market.','The seller offers chestnuts to passers-by.'),C('vendor.s2','供货商','The vendor that supplied the hospital’s software agreed to fix the login problem.','為醫院提供軟體的供應商同意修復登入問題。','a vendor of + product / service','Noun: a person or firm that sells a house, product, or service.','The firm sold software to the hospital.')],[M('The software vendor sold the hospital a product, but the sentence says it had no role in supplying anything.','The software vendor supplied the product that the hospital purchased.','A vendor is the seller or supplying firm, not an unrelated observer.')],[Q('vendor.q1','vendor.s1','meaning','What did the street vendor sell?','Roasted chestnuts.','A hospital login system.','A stone arch.','A street vendor sells food or small goods.'),Q('vendor.q2','vendor.s2','context','What did the software vendor agree to do?','Fix the login problem in the product it supplied.','Sell chestnuts at the station.','Repair a vase.','A vendor can be a firm selling a product or service.'),Q('vendor.q3','vendor.s1','distinction','Which person is a market vendor?','A seller with a stall offering vegetables.','A customer buying vegetables.','A nurse using hospital software.','The stallholder sells goods in the market.'),Q('vendor.q4','vendor.s2','word-choice','Choose the business-to-business use.','The vendor sold the firm a new payroll service.','A vendor roasted chestnuts on the street.','The street vendor set up a food stall.','The first names the firm supplying a service.')]);
P('venerable','From Latin venerabilis, “worthy of reverence,” based on venerari, “revere.”',[C('venerable.s1','受尊敬','The venerable botanist continued advising younger researchers after sixty years in the field.','這位德高望重的植物學家從事研究六十年後，仍持續指導年輕研究者。','a venerable person / tradition / institution','Adjective: commanding respect through age, tradition, or achievement.','Her long record of work earns respect.')],[M('The venerable institution was respected by nobody and had no history or achievements.','The obscure institution was respected by nobody and had no history or achievements.','Something commanding no respect is not venerable.')],[Q('venerable.q1','venerable.s1','meaning','Why was the botanist venerable?','Decades of achievement earned respect.','She had no experience or work.','She sold plants at the market.','Venerable describes someone respected through age or achievement.'),Q('venerable.q2','venerable.s1','context','Which building might be venerable?','A centuries-old library respected for its history.','A new shed with no known history.','A temporary tent on a road.','Its age and tradition command respect.'),Q('venerable.q3','venerable.s1','distinction','What does venerable imply about a tradition?','It commands respect because of its age or history.','It is a new fashion no one knows.','It is used to sell vegetables.','Long tradition can make something venerable.'),Q('venerable.q4','venerable.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','a venerable scholar admired for lifelong work','a venerable novice with no experience or achievement','a venerable vendor selling chestnuts','The scholar’s achievements command respect.')]);
P('venerate','From Latin venerari, “regard with reverence,” based on Venus, the Roman goddess of love.',[C('venerate.s1','尊敬','The community continues to venerate the teacher who established its first school.','社區仍敬重那位創辦第一所學校的教師。','venerate + person / tradition','Transitive verb: regard a person or tradition with deep respect.','The community honours the teacher’s contribution.'),C('venerate.s2','奉为神圣','Worshippers venerate the saint at a shrine dedicated to her life.','信眾在紀念那位聖人的神龕前尊奉她。','venerate a saint / sacred object','Transitive verb: treat a saint or holy thing as sacred and worthy of worship.','The saint is treated as holy.')],[M('The community venerated the teacher by publicly mocking her work and refusing to acknowledge her contribution.','The community criticized the teacher by publicly mocking her work and refusing to acknowledge her contribution.','Mockery and refusal to honour someone are not veneration.')],[Q('venerate.q1','venerate.s1','meaning','Why does the community venerate the teacher?','She founded the community’s first school.','She mocked the students.','She sold the school building.','This sense is deep respect for a person’s contribution.'),Q('venerate.q2','venerate.s2','context','What do worshippers do at the shrine?','Treat the saint as sacred and worthy of worship.','Sell the saint’s books at a market.','Ignore the shrine and its meaning.','The religious sense means regard as holy.'),Q('venerate.q3','venerate.s1','distinction','Which action venerates a tradition?','Preserving and honouring it with deep respect.','Ridiculing it in public.','Forgetting it deliberately.','Veneration involves respect and honour.'),Q('venerate.q4','venerate.s2','word-choice','Choose the sacred-use sentence.','The pilgrims venerate the relic as holy.','The museum vendor sells a souvenir.','The residents vary their opinions.','The relic is treated as sacred.')]);
P('veneration','From venerate + -ation, the feeling or act of treating someone or something as holy or highly honoured.',[C('veneration.s1','崇敬','The villagers showed veneration for the healer by preserving her clinic as a community museum.','村民保存了治療師的診所作為社區博物館，以表達崇敬。','show / feel veneration for + person / sacred thing','Noun: a feeling or act of regarding someone as holy or highly honoured.','Preserving the clinic expresses respect for her work.')],[M('The villagers showed veneration for the healer by destroying the clinic and ridiculing her work.','The villagers showed contempt for the healer by destroying the clinic and ridiculing her work.','Destroying the clinic and mocking the healer show contempt, not veneration.')],[Q('veneration.q1','veneration.s1','meaning','How did villagers show veneration for the healer?','They preserved her clinic as a museum.','They destroyed the clinic.','They mocked her work.','Veneration is deep respect or honour.'),Q('veneration.q2','veneration.s1','context','Which act shows veneration for a historical figure?','Maintaining a memorial that honours the person’s work.','Defacing the memorial to insult the person.','Selling unrelated food nearby.','The memorial expresses high regard.'),Q('veneration.q3','veneration.s1','distinction','What feeling is veneration closest to?','Reverent respect.','Angry opposition.','Casual indifference.','Veneration means regarding someone as highly honoured or holy.'),Q('veneration.q4','veneration.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','veneration for the founder of the school','veneration against the new road','veneration of a vehicle speed','The noun commonly takes for when naming the honoured person.')]);
P('vengeance','From Old French vengeance, based on venger, “avenge,” from Latin vindicare.',[C('vengeance.s1','报复','The novel’s hero sought vengeance for the betrayal but eventually chose to testify instead.','小說主角曾想為背叛尋求報復，但最後選擇作證。','seek / take vengeance for + wrong','Noun: the act of punishing or harming someone in return for what they did.','The motive is retaliation for a past wrong.')],[M('He took vengeance on the thief by forgiving him and refusing to punish or harm him.','He forgave the thief instead of taking vengeance on him.','Forgiveness without retaliation is not vengeance.')],[Q('vengeance.q1','vengeance.s1','meaning','What did the hero originally seek?','Retaliation for the betrayal.','A public holiday.','A way to repair a plant.','Vengeance is punishment in return for a wrong.'),Q('vengeance.q2','vengeance.s1','context','Which action is vengeance?','Someone harms a rival to repay an earlier injury.','Someone forgives a rival and makes peace.','Someone reports a fact truthfully.','The first is retaliation for a past wrong.'),Q('vengeance.q3','vengeance.s1','distinction','What is the usual motive for vengeance?','A desire to punish someone for a harm they caused.','A wish to reward someone for kindness.','A need to ventilate a room.','Vengeance responds to an earlier wrong.'),Q('vengeance.q4','vengeance.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','seek vengeance for the betrayal','seek a venue for the betrayal','seek a verbatim revenge','Vengeance is the act of retaliation.')]);
P('venom','From Latin venenum, “poison or drug”; it can mean animal poison or figurative bitterness.',[C('venom.s1','动物毒液','The snake’s venom entered the tissue through its fangs, so the hikers called emergency services.','蛇毒經由毒牙進入組織，健行者因此呼叫緊急救援。','venom from a snake / spider','Noun: poisonous liquid injected by an animal such as a snake or spider.','The poison is delivered by a bite.'),C('venom.s2','恶意言辞','The columnist responded to criticism with venom, accusing the reviewer of deliberate dishonesty.','專欄作家以尖刻惡意的言辭回應批評，指控評論者故意說謊。','speak / reply with venom','Noun: bitter feeling that shows a desire to hurt people.','The reply is hostile and intended to wound.')],[M('The snake injected venom by delivering harmless flower nectar through its fangs.','The snake injected venom, a poisonous liquid, through its fangs.','Venom is poison delivered through a bite, not harmless nectar.')],[Q('venom.q1','venom.s1','meaning','What entered the hiker’s tissue?','Poison delivered by the snake’s fangs.','A harmless flower nectar.','A spoken accusation.','Animal venom is a poisonous liquid injected by a bite or sting.'),Q('venom.q2','venom.s2','context','How did the columnist answer criticism?','With bitter, hostile language intended to hurt.','With a neutral scientific report.','With a snake bite.','Figurative venom describes hateful bitterness.'),Q('venom.q3','venom.s1','distinction','Which use is literal?','A spider injects venom into its prey.','A speaker answers with venom.','A critic writes a bitter reply.','The first refers to biological poison.'),Q('venom.q4','venom.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative sense.','Her reply dripped with venom.','The snake’s venom affected the tissue.','The spider delivered venom through a sting.','The reply uses venom to mean bitter hostility.')]);
P('venomous','From venom + -ous; it describes an animal that produces poison or speech intended to hurt.',[C('venomous.s1','有毒生物','The venomous spider delivered a painful sting when the camper disturbed its web.','露營者驚動蛛網後，這隻有毒蜘蛛螫了他，造成疼痛。','a venomous snake / spider / bite','Adjective: producing poison that harms through a bite or sting.','The spider’s sting injects poison.'),C('venomous.s2','恶毒言辞','Her venomous comments targeted the new employee’s accent rather than the quality of the work.','她惡毒的評論針對新員工的口音，而不是工作品質。','a venomous remark / attack','Adjective: full of hatred and intended to hurt feelings.','The comments are personally hostile.')],[M('The venomous spider was harmless because it produced no poison and could not sting.','The harmless spider produced no poison and could not sting.','An animal producing no poison is not venomous.')],[Q('venomous.q1','venomous.s1','meaning','Why was the spider venomous?','Its sting could deliver poison.','It produced no poison and could not sting.','It attacked someone with words.','Venomous describes animals producing harmful poison.'),Q('venomous.q2','venomous.s2','context','Why were her comments called venomous?','They were hateful remarks meant to hurt a colleague.','They were a neutral description of work.','They were a spider’s sting.','The figurative sense means hostile and hurtful.'),Q('venomous.q3','venomous.s1','distinction','Which is a venomous animal?','A snake whose bite injects poison.','A harmless turtle that cannot bite.','A flower with no sting.','The snake delivers venom through its bite.'),Q('venomous.q4','venomous.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','a venomous insult about his family','a venomous snake in the grass','a venomous spider sting','The insult is hateful and intended to hurt.')]);
P('vent','From Latin ventus, “wind,” via French; it can be an opening, the release of feelings, or the act of providing an air passage.',[C('vent.s1','通风口','Smoke escaped through a narrow vent near the top of the laboratory wall.','煙從實驗室牆壁上方的狹窄通風口排出。','an air / smoke vent','Noun: an opening that lets air, gas, or smoke pass out.','The opening releases smoke.'),C('vent.s2','发泄情绪','After the meeting, Jo vented her frustration to a trusted colleague.','會議後，喬向信任的同事發洩自己的挫折感。','vent anger / frustration to + person','Verb: express anger or another strong feeling so it comes out.','She puts the feeling into words.'),C('vent.s3','设置通道','The engineer vented the tank so expanding gas could escape safely.','工程師為儲槽設置排氣通道，讓膨脹的氣體能安全逸出。','vent + room / tank / gas','Transitive verb: provide a passage for air or gas.','The tank receives an outlet for gas.')],[M('Smoke escaped through a vent, but the wall had no opening or passage for gas at all.','Smoke escaped through a gap in the wall, not through a vent.','A vent is an opening or passage through which gas can escape.')],[Q('vent.q1','vent.s1','meaning','How did smoke leave the laboratory?','Through an opening near the top of the wall.','Through a sealed solid wall.','Through a spoken complaint.','A vent is an opening for air, gas, or smoke.'),Q('vent.q2','vent.s2','context','What did Jo do after the meeting?','Expressed her frustration to someone she trusted.','Opened a tank to release gas.','Closed the wall opening.','Vent can mean express a strong feeling.'),Q('vent.q3','vent.s3','distinction','Why did the engineer vent the tank?','To provide an escape passage for expanding gas.','To complain about the meeting.','To install a bank vault.','The verb means provide a passage for gas.'),Q('vent.q4','vent.s1','word-choice','Choose the opening sense.','The attic vent released warm air.','He vented his anger after work.','The mechanic vented the fuel tank.','The attic vent is a physical opening.')]);
P('ventilate','From Latin ventilare, “fan or expose to air”; it means bring fresh air into a room or make an idea public for discussion.',[C('ventilate.s1','换气','Open the windows to ventilate the classroom after the science experiment.','科學實驗後打開窗戶，讓教室通風。','ventilate a room / building','Transitive verb: cause fresh air to enter and move through a room.','Opening windows replaces stale air.'),C('ventilate.s2','公开讨论','The chair invited residents to ventilate their concerns about the housing plan at the public meeting.','主席邀請居民在公開會議上提出並討論對住房計畫的疑慮。','ventilate a concern / idea publicly','Transitive verb: make a complaint or idea public so people can discuss it.','Residents can openly discuss their concerns.')],[M('The teacher ventilated the classroom by sealing every window and preventing fresh air from entering.','The teacher closed the windows and left the classroom unventilated.','Sealing the windows prevents ventilation rather than ventilating the room.')],[Q('ventilate.q1','ventilate.s1','meaning','What should the teacher do after the experiment?','Bring fresh air through the classroom.','Seal every window.','Discuss the housing plan.','Ventilate a room means make fresh air circulate.'),Q('ventilate.q2','ventilate.s2','context','Why did the chair invite residents to ventilate concerns?','To make their concerns public for discussion.','To remove smoke from a room.','To build a ventilator.','The figurative sense is openly discuss an idea or complaint.'),Q('ventilate.q3','ventilate.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses ventilate literally?','The crew ventilated the tunnel with fresh air.','The committee ventilated its objections in public.','Residents ventilated their concerns at the meeting.','The tunnel receives moving fresh air.'),Q('ventilate.q4','ventilate.s2','word-choice','Choose the public-discussion sense.','The forum let parents ventilate their concerns.','The nurse ventilated the room after cleaning.','A fan ventilated the laboratory.','The forum makes concerns open to discussion.')]);
P('ventilation','From ventilate + -ion; it can mean moving fresh air or publicly discussing an issue.',[C('ventilation.s1','空气流通','Good ventilation kept the crowded kitchen cool while the ovens were running.','烤箱運轉時，良好的通風讓擁擠的廚房保持涼爽。','ventilation in / of + room','Noun: movement of fresh air through a room or building.','Air moves through the kitchen and removes heat.'),C('ventilation.s2','公开讨论','The public hearing provided ventilation of the residents’ concerns about rent increases.','公開聽證會讓居民能公開討論租金上漲的疑慮。','ventilation of + issue / concern','Noun: open and public discussion of a problem or question.','The hearing lets people raise the issue openly.')],[M('The kitchen had good ventilation, although no air moved in or out and the room remained sealed.','The kitchen had poor ventilation because no air moved in or out.','Ventilation requires movement of fresh air through a space.')],[Q('ventilation.q1','ventilation.s1','meaning','Why was the kitchen comfortable?','Fresh air moved through it and carried heat away.','It was sealed with no air movement.','The residents held a meeting there.','Ventilation is air movement through a room.'),Q('ventilation.q2','ventilation.s2','context','What did the public hearing provide?','An open discussion of residents’ concerns.','A fan to cool the kitchen.','A way to seal the windows.','This sense means public discussion.'),Q('ventilation.q3','ventilation.s1','distinction','Which feature improves ventilation?','An exhaust fan that removes stale air.','A sealed window with no airflow.','A locked bank vault.','The fan moves air through the room.'),Q('ventilation.q4','ventilation.s2','word-choice','Choose the discussion use.','ventilation of the issue at an open hearing','ventilation through a kitchen fan','ventilation of smoke from a tunnel','The hearing provides public discussion of the issue.')]);
P('ventilator','From ventilate + -or; it names an opening or fan for air, or a medical machine that moves air in and out of lungs.',[C('ventilator.s1','通风设备或医疗机器','The hospital connected a ventilator to help the patient breathe while the infection was treated.','治療感染期間，醫院連接呼吸器協助病人呼吸。','a medical / wall ventilator','Noun: an air opening or fan, or a machine that moves air in and out of the lungs.','The medical device supports breathing.')],[M('The ventilator helped the patient breathe by blocking all airflow and preventing air from entering the lungs.','The ventilator helped the patient breathe by moving air in and out of the lungs.','A ventilator supports breathing by moving air, not by blocking it.')],[Q('ventilator.q1','ventilator.s1','meaning','How did the hospital ventilator help the patient?','It moved air in and out of the lungs.','It blocked all airflow.','It measured the patient’s height.','A medical ventilator supports breathing.'),Q('ventilator.q2','ventilator.s1','context','Which device could ventilate a bathroom?','A fan that removes stale air.','A sealed door with no airflow.','A velvet curtain.','A ventilator can be an opening or fan for fresh air.'),Q('ventilator.q3','ventilator.s1','distinction','What does a medical ventilator do?','Assists breathing by moving air.','Carries blood through veins.','Makes a public complaint.','The machine moves air in and out of lungs.'),Q('ventilator.q4','ventilator.s1','word-choice','Choose the medical use.','Doctors placed the patient on a ventilator.','The engineer opened the attic vent.','Residents ventilated concerns at the meeting.','The medical machine supports breathing.')]);
P('venture','From Latin ventura, “about to happen,” through Old French; it can be a risky undertaking, a daring action, or a tentative statement.',[C('venture.s1','冒险事业','Their first renewable-energy venture required a large loan and could still fail.','他們第一項再生能源事業需要大筆貸款，仍可能失敗。','a business / risky venture','Noun: a new business or journey that may fail and costs effort or money.','The project involves risk and investment.'),C('venture.s2','冒险前往','Few climbers ventured beyond the marked trail after dark.','天黑後，很少有登山者敢越過標記步道。','venture into / beyond + place','Verb: go somewhere or do something though it may be dangerous.','The climbers take a risk by going past the trail.'),C('venture.s3','试探性提出','“Perhaps we should postpone,” she ventured, unsure whether the chair would agree.','她不確定主席是否同意，便試探性地提出：「也許我們該延期。」','venture + speech / an opinion','Verb: say something when unsure it will be welcome.','She cautiously offers a possibly unwelcome opinion.')],[M('The climbers ventured beyond the marked trail by staying safely on the path and never leaving it.','The climbers stayed on the marked trail rather than venturing beyond it.','Remaining on the path is not venturing beyond it.')],[Q('venture.q1','venture.s1','meaning','Why was the renewable-energy project a venture?','It was a new business effort with financial risk.','It was guaranteed to succeed without cost.','It was a public hearing.','A venture may fail and requires investment or effort.'),Q('venture.q2','venture.s2','context','What did the climbers do after dark?','Some dared to go beyond the marked trail.','They stayed safely on the trail.','They opened a bank vault.','Venture can mean go somewhere despite risk.'),Q('venture.q3','venture.s3','distinction','How did she use venture in the meeting?','She cautiously offered a suggestion that might not be welcome.','She launched a new energy company.','She climbed beyond a trail.','The speech sense is to say something tentatively.'),Q('venture.q4','venture.s1','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','Their new shop was a risky venture.','They ventured into the forest.','She ventured a suggestion at the meeting.','The shop is a new enterprise that could fail.')]);
P('venturesome','From venture + -some, describing someone daring or something that involves risk.',[C('venturesome.s1','大胆冒险','A venturesome photographer crossed the narrow ridge to capture the sunrise from the western side.','一位大膽的攝影師越過狹窄山脊，從西側拍攝日出。','a venturesome person / plan / journey','Adjective: daring or involving risk.','The photographer takes a risky route for the picture.')],[M('The venturesome route was completely safe, required no daring, and involved no risk at all.','The routine route was completely safe, required no daring, and involved no risk at all.','A route involving no risk is not venturesome.')],[Q('venturesome.q1','venturesome.s1','meaning','Why was the photographer venturesome?','The photographer crossed a narrow, risky ridge.','The photographer stayed indoors.','The route involved no risk or daring.','Venturesome means daring or risky.'),Q('venturesome.q2','venturesome.s1','context','Which plan is venturesome?','Sailing beyond the charted coast in unsettled weather.','Walking a marked indoor hallway.','Taking a familiar bus route.','The voyage involves risk.'),Q('venturesome.q3','venturesome.s1','distinction','What quality does venturesome praise?','Willingness to take a daring risk.','Fear of every new activity.','A clear written statement.','The word describes boldness.'),Q('venturesome.q4','venturesome.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','a venturesome expedition across uncharted ice','a venturesome stroll on a safe, flat path','a venturesome answer copied from a form','The expedition is daring and risky.')]);
P('venue','From Latin venire, “come,” through Old French venue; it means an event location or the place where a case is heard.',[C('venue.s1','活动地点','The school chose a larger venue for the concert after ticket sales exceeded expectations.','售票超出預期後，學校為音樂會選擇了更大的場地。','a venue for + event','Noun: the place chosen for a concert, match, meeting, or wedding.','The building hosts the concert.'),C('venue.s2','审理地点','The judge changed the venue of the trial so an impartial jury could be selected.','法官更改了審判地點，以便選出公正陪審團。','change / set the venue of a trial','Noun: the place where a court case is heard.','The case will be heard in another location.')],[M('The concert venue was the song the orchestra played rather than the hall where it performed.','The concert venue was the hall where the orchestra performed.','A venue is a place for the event, not the music itself.')],[Q('venue.q1','venue.s1','meaning','Why did the school choose a larger venue?','More people wanted tickets for the concert.','The court needed a new jury.','The orchestra changed its song.','A venue is the event’s location.'),Q('venue.q2','venue.s2','context','Why did the judge change the trial venue?','To allow selection of an impartial jury at another place.','To find a larger concert hall.','To choose a different court verdict.','The legal sense is where a case is heard.'),Q('venue.q3','venue.s1','distinction','Which is a wedding venue?','A hall where the ceremony and reception take place.','The couple’s wedding song.','The judge’s opinion about a case.','The hall is the event location.'),Q('venue.q4','venue.s2','word-choice','Choose the legal use.','The court moved the venue of the hearing.','The band booked a venue for its concert.','The school selected a venue for the match.','The first concerns where a case is heard.')]);
P('Venus','From Latin Venus, the Roman goddess of love and beauty; the planet was named for the bright goddess.',[C('Venus.s1','行星','Venus appeared as a bright point above the western horizon shortly after sunset.','日落後不久，金星像明亮光點出現在西方地平線上。','the planet Venus','Proper noun: the second planet from the Sun, often shining brightly in the sky.','The planet is visible in the evening sky.'),C('Venus.s2','罗马女神','The Roman statue depicts Venus holding an apple, a symbol associated with the goddess.','這尊羅馬雕像描繪維納斯手持蘋果，這是與女神相關的象徵。','the goddess Venus','Proper noun: the Roman goddess of love and beauty.','The statue represents the deity.')],[M('Venus is the second planet from the Sun and the Roman goddess of love, but the sentence calls it a North American sports team.','Venus is the second planet from the Sun and the Roman goddess of love and beauty.','Venus names the planet or the Roman goddess, not a sports team in this entry.')],[Q('Venus.q1','Venus.s1','meaning','What appeared above the western horizon after sunset?','The planet Venus.','The Roman statue.','A school varsity team.','Venus is the second planet from the Sun and can shine brightly.'),Q('Venus.q2','Venus.s2','context','Who does the statue depict?','The Roman goddess of love and beauty.','The planet’s orbit.','A theatre usher.','The goddess Venus is the Roman deity.'),Q('Venus.q3','Venus.s1','distinction','Which Venus is visible in the evening sky?','The planet, the second from the Sun.','The goddess as a physical planet.','A Roman statue on a museum shelf.','The bright point is the planet.'),Q('Venus.q4','Venus.s2','word-choice','Choose the mythological use.','The sculptor carved Venus with an apple.','Venus rose above the western horizon.','The spacecraft entered Venus’s orbit.','The first refers to the goddess represented in sculpture.')]);
P('veracious','From Latin verax, “truthful,” based on verus, “true”; it describes a truthful speaker or a statement that matches fact.',[C('veracious.s1','真实可信','The veracious witness corrected her own earlier mistake and gave a consistent account.','這位誠實的證人更正了先前的錯誤，並提供一致的敘述。','a veracious witness / account','Adjective: speaking the truth or conforming to fact.','The account is truthful and accurate.')],[M('The witness was veracious because she knowingly invented every detail of the account.','The witness was deceptive because she knowingly invented every detail of the account.','Knowingly inventing details is not speaking truthfully.')],[Q('veracious.q1','veracious.s1','meaning','Why was the witness called veracious?','She corrected an error and gave a truthful account.','She invented every detail knowingly.','She refused to answer all questions.','Veracious means truthful or conforming to fact.'),Q('veracious.q2','veracious.s1','context','Which report is veracious?','A report that matches the records and evidence.','A report that contradicts every verified fact.','A report that invents a quotation.','A veracious account conforms to fact.'),Q('veracious.q3','veracious.s1','distinction','Which person is veracious?','A speaker who admits a mistake and tells what happened.','A speaker who knowingly lies.','A person who remains silent.','The first speaks truthfully.'),Q('veracious.q4','veracious.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','a veracious account of the events','a veracious lie invented to deceive','a veracious rumor with no factual basis','A truthful account conforms to facts.')]);
P('veracity','From veracious + -ity, from Latin verax, “truthful”; it names the truth of statements or the habit of telling truth.',[C('veracity.s1','陈述真实性','The editor checked the veracity of the quotation against the original recording.','編輯把引文與原始錄音核對，以確認其真實性。','the veracity of + claim / report','Noun: the quality of statements being true and accurate.','The quote is checked for factual accuracy.'),C('veracity.s2','诚实品格','The court trusted the witness’s veracity because she had been truthful in earlier testimony.','法院相信證人的誠實品格，因為她先前作證時一直誠實。','a person of veracity; question someone’s veracity','Noun: the habit or quality of telling the truth.','The witness has a record of honesty.')],[M('The editor confirmed the quotation’s veracity by showing it did not match the recording at all.','The editor questioned the quotation’s veracity because it did not match the recording.','A quotation that conflicts with the source has questionable truthfulness.')],[Q('veracity.q1','veracity.s1','meaning','What did the editor check?','Whether the quotation matched the original recording.','The speaker’s clothing.','The recording’s venue.','Veracity can mean truth and accuracy of a statement.'),Q('veracity.q2','veracity.s2','context','Why did the court trust the witness?','The witness had a record of telling the truth.','The witness changed every statement.','The witness sold goods at a market.','This sense concerns a person’s truthfulness.'),Q('veracity.q3','veracity.s1','distinction','Which question concerns a claim’s veracity?','Is the claim accurate according to the original data?','Does the claim sound colourful?','Who owns the microphone?','Veracity tests whether a statement is true.'),Q('veracity.q4','veracity.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about honesty as a personal quality.','Her veracity made her a trusted witness.','The editor checked the veracity of the quotation.','The report’s veracity depended on a recording.','The first describes the person’s habit of truth-telling.')]);
P('veranda','Borrowed through Portuguese varanda, “balcony or gallery”; the word ultimately has a longer South Asian history.',[C('veranda.s1','有顶外廊','They ate breakfast on the veranda, sheltered from the morning rain.','他們在游廊上吃早餐，避開清晨的雨。','sit / eat on the veranda','Noun: a roofed platform with open sides along the outside of a house.','The meal is on a roofed area attached to the exterior.')],[M('The family ate on the veranda, a sealed room entirely inside the house with no outside opening.','The family ate on the veranda, a roofed open-sided platform along the outside of the house.','A veranda is attached to the exterior and is not a sealed interior room.')],[Q('veranda.q1','veranda.s1','meaning','Where did the family eat breakfast?','On a roofed open-sided platform outside the house.','In a sealed room deep inside the house.','On the roof of a moving bus.','A veranda is an exterior sheltered gallery.'),Q('veranda.q2','veranda.s1','context','Which feature makes a porch-like space a veranda?','It is attached to the house and has a roof with open sides.','It is a windowless room under the ground.','It is a detached storage shed.','The source sense specifies a roofed exterior platform.'),Q('veranda.q3','veranda.s1','distinction','Which plan uses a veranda naturally?','Place chairs on the covered gallery along the garden side of the house.','Put chairs in a locked basement with no exterior wall.','Build a freestanding tent across the road.','A veranda adjoins the outside of a building.'),Q('veranda.q4','veranda.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate description.','A roofed, open-sided gallery runs along the house.','A roofless cellar lies under the kitchen.','A hallway separates two rooms indoors.','The first describes a veranda.')]);
P('verb','From Latin verbum, “word”; in grammar a verb expresses an action, event, or state.',[C('verb.s1','动词','In “The children laughed,” laughed is the verb that names their action.','在“The children laughed”中，laughed 是表示孩子们动作的动词。','identify / conjugate a verb','Noun: a word that names an action, event, or state.','The word laughed names what the children did.'),C('verb.s2','谓语核心','In “She has finished,” finished is the main verb and changes the clause’s tense.','在“She has finished”中，finished 是主要动词，决定从句的时态。','the main / finite verb','Noun: a clause word that changes for tense and agrees with its subject.','The verb form participates in tense and subject agreement.')],[M('In “The children laughed,” children is the verb and laughed is the subject.','In “The children laughed,” laughed is the verb and children is the subject.','The noun children names the subject; laughed expresses the action.')],[Q('verb.q1','verb.s1','meaning','Which word is the verb in “The children laughed”?','laughed','children','the','The verb names the action in this sentence.'),Q('verb.q2','verb.s2','context','What does the main verb help show in “She has finished”?','The clause’s tense and the action completed by the subject.','The colour of the subject.','The number of paragraphs in the text.','The verb is the clause word that changes for tense.'),Q('verb.q3','verb.s1','distinction','Which item is a verb rather than a noun?','decide','decision','decisive','Decide names an action and is a verb.'),Q('verb.q4','verb.s2','grammar','In “They were waiting,” which word is the main lexical verb?','waiting','They','the comma','Waiting carries the action while were marks tense/aspect.')]);
P('verbal','From Latin verbalis, based on verbum, “word”; it can mean spoken or relating to words and verbs.',[C('verbal.s1','口头的','The buyer and seller made a verbal agreement, then put the terms in writing.','買方和賣方先達成口頭協議，之後再把條款寫下來。','a verbal agreement / warning','Adjective: spoken rather than written, or communicated by words.','The agreement was first made in speech.'),C('verbal.s2','言语或语法动词的','The test measures verbal ability, while a separate section tests numerical reasoning.','這項測驗評量語言能力，另一部分則測試數字推理。','verbal ability; verbal form','Adjective: relating to words or, in grammar, to verbs.','The ability concerns language rather than numerical reasoning.')],[M('They signed a verbal agreement without speaking or using any words.','They signed a written agreement without speaking or using any words.','Verbal communication uses spoken words; a silent signed document is written.')],[Q('verbal.q1','verbal.s1','meaning','How was the agreement first made?','The parties discussed it aloud.','They exchanged only silent gestures.','They wrote it without speaking.','Verbal can mean spoken rather than written.'),Q('verbal.q2','verbal.s2','context','What does a verbal ability test assess?','Skill with language and words.','Skill at measuring temperature.','The ability to repair a vehicle.','This sense relates to words.'),Q('verbal.q3','verbal.s2','distinction','In grammar, what can verbal describe?','A form or construction related to a verb.','A roofed gallery.','A jury’s final decision.','The grammatical sense concerns verbs.'),Q('verbal.q4','verbal.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase meaning “spoken, not written.”','a verbal warning given in person','a written notice sent by post','a numerical chart with no words','A verbal warning is communicated in speech.')]);
P('verbalizable','From verbalize + -able, “capable of being expressed in words.”',[C('verbalizable.s1','能用语言表达的','The patient found the source of the discomfort verbalizable after the doctor asked specific questions.','醫生提出具體問題後，病人發現自己能用言語描述不適的來源。','verbalizable thoughts / feelings','Adjective: able to be expressed in language.','The patient can put the experience into words.')],[M('Her verbalizable concern could not possibly be put into words or described in language.','Her ineffable concern could not be put into words or described in language.','Something that cannot be expressed in words is not verbalizable.')],[Q('verbalizable.q1','verbalizable.s1','meaning','What happened to the patient’s concern after the questions?','The patient could describe it in words.','The patient forgot how to speak.','The concern became a courtroom verdict.','Verbalizable means capable of being expressed in language.'),Q('verbalizable.q2','verbalizable.s1','context','Which feeling is verbalizable?','A feeling someone can explain with words.','A feeling that cannot be named or described at all.','A number written on a chart.','The word applies when language can express the feeling.'),Q('verbalizable.q3','verbalizable.s1','distinction','What is the opposite description of a verbalizable idea?','One that is impossible to put into words.','One that is easy to state clearly.','One that has already been explained.','If it cannot be put into words, it is not verbalizable.'),Q('verbalizable.q4','verbalizable.s1','word-choice','Choose the sentence using verbalizable correctly.','After reflection, his vague unease became verbalizable.','The verbalizable silence could never be described in words.','She verbalizable the thought yesterday.','The first describes a thought that can now be expressed.')]);
P('verbalize','From verbal + -ize, formed on Latin verbum, “word”; it means put a thought or feeling into words.',[C('verbalize.s1','用言语表达','The coach asked each player to verbalize one concern before the team changed its plan.','教練要求每位隊員在改變計畫前說出一項顧慮。','verbalize a thought / feeling / concern','Verb: express thoughts or feelings in speech or writing.','Each player is asked to put a concern into words.')],[M('The coach asked her to verbalize her concern, so she kept it entirely unspoken and refused to express it.','The coach asked her to verbalize her concern, so she explained it aloud.','Keeping a concern unspoken does not verbalize it.')],[Q('verbalize.q1','verbalize.s1','meaning','What did the coach ask each player to do?','Put one concern into words.','Keep every concern secret and unspoken.','Write a legal verdict.','To verbalize is to express something in language.'),Q('verbalize.q2','verbalize.s1','context','Which action verbalizes a feeling?','Saying, “I feel anxious about the deadline.”','Ignoring the feeling and saying nothing.','Measuring the room’s height.','The speaker expresses the feeling in words.'),Q('verbalize.q3','verbalize.s1','distinction','Which verb is closest in meaning to verbalize here?','articulate','conceal','estimate','Articulate means express clearly in words.'),Q('verbalize.q4','verbalize.s1','grammar','Which sentence uses verbalize with a direct object?','She verbalized her doubts to the team.','Her verbalizable doubt was quiet.','They reached a verbal agreement.','Her doubts are the direct object of verbalized.')]);
P('verbally','From verbal + -ly; it means by speaking, or in relation to words rather than another medium.',[C('verbally.s1','口头地','The landlord verbally approved the repair, but the tenant requested written confirmation.','房東口頭同意了維修，但房客要求書面確認。','agree / warn / report verbally','Adverb: by spoken words rather than in writing.','Approval was spoken and not yet documented.'),C('verbally.s1','用词语地','The two proposals are verbally similar but differ in their numerical assumptions.','這兩項提案在措辭上相似，但數字假設不同。','verbally similar / skilled','Adverb: in terms of words or language.','The comparison concerns wording, not the numbers.')],[M('The landlord verbally approved the work in a signed written document but never spoke or used words.','The landlord approved the work in writing but did not approve it verbally.','A silent written approval is not an approval made by speaking.')],[Q('verbally.q1','verbally.s1','meaning','How did the landlord first approve the repair?','By saying aloud that it could go ahead.','By signing a form without speaking.','By changing the rent figure.','Verbally means by spoken words.'),Q('verbally.q2','verbally.s1','context','In what way were the proposals verbally similar?','Their wording was alike.','Their prices were exactly equal.','They were both spoken aloud at the same time.','Verbally can refer to language or wording.'),Q('verbally.q3','verbally.s1','distinction','Which report was delivered verbally?','A witness described the event aloud at the meeting.','A clerk emailed a written account only.','A machine printed a chart without text.','The first report uses spoken words.'),Q('verbally.q4','verbally.s1','grammar','What does verbally modify in “They agreed verbally”?','The manner in which they agreed.','The number of people in the room.','The agreement’s colour.','The adverb describes how the agreement was made.')]);
P('verbatim','From Latin verbatim, “word for word,” based on verbum, “word.”',[C('verbatim.s1','逐字地','The court reporter transcribed the witness’s answer verbatim, preserving every hesitation.','法庭記錄員逐字記下證人的回答，保留了每次停頓。','quote / copy / repeat verbatim','Adverb: using exactly the same words, without alteration.','The transcript preserves the witness’s exact wording.'),C('verbatim.s2','逐字的','The archive contains a verbatim record of the minister’s speech.','檔案館保存著部長演說的逐字紀錄。','a verbatim transcript / record','Adjective: recording or giving the exact words spoken or written.','The record contains the original words.')],[M('The transcript was verbatim, although the editor replaced every sentence with a new paraphrase.','The transcript was a paraphrase, because the editor replaced the original wording.','A paraphrase changes the wording, so it is not verbatim.')],[Q('verbatim.q1','verbatim.s1','meaning','What did the court reporter preserve?','The witness’s exact words, including hesitations.','A shortened summary only.','The witness’s clothing.','Verbatim means word for word without changes.'),Q('verbatim.q2','verbatim.s2','context','What is a verbatim record of a speech?','A record containing the exact words spoken.','A loose summary with new wording.','A list of the speaker’s future appointments.','The adjective describes an exact-word record.'),Q('verbatim.q3','verbatim.s1','distinction','How does a verbatim quotation differ from a paraphrase?','It keeps the source’s wording exactly.','It replaces the source’s wording with a summary.','It omits the source entirely.','A paraphrase changes wording; verbatim does not.'),Q('verbatim.q4','verbatim.s2','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','a verbatim transcript of the interview','a verbatim summary written in entirely new words','a verbatim guess about what was said','A transcript can record the exact words.')]);
P('verbiage','From French verbiage, from verbe, “word,” plus -age; it can mean excessive wording or simply wording in a text.',[C('verbiage.s1','冗长用语','The editor removed legal verbiage that obscured the simple payment rule.','編輯刪去遮蔽簡單付款規則的法律冗詞。','cut / reduce / excessive verbiage','Noun: speech or writing using more words than necessary; sometimes the wording itself.','The extra language hides the rule.')],[M('The editor reduced the verbiage by adding three unnecessary pages of repetitive explanations.','The editor reduced the verbiage by deleting repetitive explanations.','Adding unnecessary repetitive pages increases verbiage rather than reducing it.')],[Q('verbiage.q1','verbiage.s1','meaning','Why did the editor remove some language?','It used too many words and obscured the rule.','It was a roofed outdoor gallery.','It was a one-word answer.','Verbiage often means excessive or needlessly complex wording.'),Q('verbiage.q2','verbiage.s1','context','Which document contains too much verbiage?','A short policy buried under pages of repetitive clauses.','A clear one-sentence instruction.','A table containing only figures.','Excessive wording is verbiage.'),Q('verbiage.q3','verbiage.s1','distinction','What is the editor most likely to do about verbiage?','Cut unnecessary phrases.','Add several repetitions of each sentence.','Replace the document with a photograph.','Reducing verbiage means removing unnecessary wording.'),Q('verbiage.q4','verbiage.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','The contract’s verbiage made a simple fee difficult to understand.','The verbiage was a narrow strip beside the road.','She verbiaged the contract yesterday.','Verbiage is a noun for wording, often excessive wording.')]);
P('verdict','From Anglo-French verdit, “true saying,” from ver, “true,” and dit, “said.”',[C('verdict.s1','陪审团裁决','After reviewing the evidence, the jury returned a unanimous verdict of not guilty.','審閱證據後，陪審團一致裁定被告無罪。','return / reach / deliver a verdict','Noun: the official decision of a jury about guilt or innocence.','The jury announces its legal decision.'),C('verdict.s2','判断；意见','The reviewer’s final verdict was that the machine was reliable but too expensive.','評論者最後的評價是，這台機器可靠但價格過高。','a verdict on + product / performance','Noun: an opinion reached after testing or considering something.','The reviewer gives a considered judgment.')],[M('The jury returned its verdict before hearing any evidence and without deciding whether the accused was guilty.','The jury delayed its verdict until it had considered the evidence.','A verdict is a jury decision made after considering the case evidence.')],[Q('verdict.q1','verdict.s1','meaning','What did the jury announce?','Its official decision about guilt.','A sports venue.','A witness’s exact transcript.','A legal verdict is a jury’s decision.'),Q('verdict.q2','verdict.s2','context','What was the reviewer’s verdict on the machine?','A considered opinion that it worked well but cost too much.','A jury’s decision about a criminal defendant.','A record of every word in a speech.','This sense means an opinion after evaluation.'),Q('verdict.q3','verdict.s1','distinction','Who typically returns a verdict in a jury trial?','The jury','The product reviewer','The court reporter','In the source sense, the jury gives the official decision.'),Q('verdict.q4','verdict.s2','word-choice','Choose the non-legal use.','Her verdict on the restaurant was that the food was excellent.','The jury reached a verdict after deliberation.','The court recorded the verdict in its file.','The restaurant review is an opinion after consideration.')]);
P('verge','From Latin virga, “rod or branch,” through Old French; it names an edge or a point close to a state, and is also used of a road-edge strip.',[C('verge.s1','临界点','The negotiations were on the verge of collapse when both sides agreed to pause.','談判瀕臨破裂時，雙方同意暫停。','on the verge of + noun / -ing','Noun: the point at which something is about to happen.','Collapse was about to happen but had not yet occurred.'),C('verge.s2','路边草地','The driver pulled onto the grass verge to let the ambulance pass.','駕駛把車停到路邊草地，讓救護車通過。','the grass / road verge','Noun: a narrow grassy strip at the side of a road.','The car stops on the strip beside the roadway.'),C('verge.s3','濒于；近乎','The joke verged on cruelty because it mocked the child’s disability.','這個笑話近乎殘忍，因為它嘲弄了孩子的身心障礙。','verge on / upon + noun','Verb: be very close to an extreme or undesirable state.','The joke approaches the boundary of cruelty.')],[M('The negotiations were on the verge of collapse after they had already collapsed and ended years earlier.','The negotiations were on the verge of collapse, with failure about to happen.','On the verge means close to an event, not long after it has already occurred.')],[Q('verge.q1','verge.s1','meaning','What was about to happen to the negotiations?','They were close to collapsing.','They had been finished for years.','They were moving onto a grassy road edge.','On the verge of means close to a state or event.'),Q('verge.q2','verge.s2','context','Where did the driver stop?','On the narrow grass strip beside the road.','At the center of a courtroom.','On a roofed gallery at home.','A road verge is a strip along the road.'),Q('verge.q3','verge.s3','distinction','What does “The comment verged on insult” mean?','It came close to being an insult.','It was a strip of grass beside a road.','It was copied word for word.','The verb verge on means approach a state.'),Q('verge.q4','verge.s1','grammar','Which phrase follows verge in the common expression?','on the verge of tears','on the verdict at tears','on a verbiage of tears','The fixed expression is on the verge of + noun or -ing.')]);
P('veridical','From Latin veridicus, “speaking truth,” based on verus, “true,” and dicere, “say.”',[C('veridical.s1','符合事实的','The archive confirmed that the witness’s memory of the meeting was veridical.','檔案證實證人對那場會議的記憶符合事實。','a veridical memory / perception','Adjective: corresponding to what is actually the case, especially of a perception or memory.','The remembered event matches the records.')],[M('Her memory was veridical even though every independently checked detail contradicted it.','Her memory was inaccurate because every independently checked detail contradicted it.','A memory contradicted by verified details does not correspond to reality.')],[Q('veridical.q1','veridical.s1','meaning','What did the archive show about the witness’s memory?','It matched the documented facts.','It contradicted every checked detail.','It was copied word for word from a poem.','Veridical means corresponding to what is actually true.'),Q('veridical.q2','veridical.s1','context','Which perception is veridical?','A reading of the gauge that matches the actual pressure.','A reading that is wrong by a factor of ten.','A guess that cannot be compared with reality.','A veridical perception corresponds to reality.'),Q('veridical.q3','veridical.s1','distinction','What kind of memory can be called veridical?','One whose content is accurate.','One whose details are all invented.','One that has been paraphrased.','The adjective means truthful or accurate to reality.'),Q('veridical.q4','veridical.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate collocation.','a veridical account of the recorded event','a veridical account that contradicts all evidence','a veridical claim no one can ever check','A veridical account agrees with what happened.')]);
P('verifiable','From verify + -able, “capable of being checked or confirmed.”',[C('verifiable.s1','可核实的','The report lists verifiable figures and links each one to the original public dataset.','報告列出可核實的數字，並把每個數字連結到原始公開資料集。','verifiable claim / evidence / data','Adjective: capable of being proved or confirmed by evidence.','Readers can check the figures against a source.')],[M('The claim was verifiable because no evidence, record, or possible test could be used to check it.','The claim was unverifiable because no evidence, record, or possible test could be used to check it.','A claim that cannot be checked is unverifiable, not verifiable.')],[Q('verifiable.q1','verifiable.s1','meaning','Why are the report’s figures verifiable?','Each can be checked against the linked dataset.','No records or tests can check any figure.','The figures are opinions with no evidence.','Verifiable means capable of confirmation by evidence.'),Q('verifiable.q2','verifiable.s1','context','Which allegation is verifiable?','One supported by records that an investigator can inspect.','One with no evidence and no possible way to test it.','One that changes whenever it is repeated.','Inspectable evidence makes a claim checkable.'),Q('verifiable.q3','verifiable.s1','distinction','What does a verifiable result allow another researcher to do?','Check it independently against evidence.','Accept it without seeing any data.','Replace it with an unrelated opinion.','The result can be tested or confirmed.'),Q('verifiable.q4','verifiable.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct description.','The timestamp is verifiable from the server log.','The timestamp is verifiable although no log or record exists.','The timestamp is verifiable because it can never be checked.','A server log supplies evidence for checking the time.')]);
P('verification','From verify + -ation, based on Latin verus, “true”; verification is the process of checking truth or correctness.',[C('verification.s1','核实过程','The bank completed identity verification before activating the new account.','銀行完成身分核驗後才啟用新帳戶。','identity / document / data verification','Noun: confirmation by examination, test, or evidence.','The bank checks identity records before approval.')],[M('Identity verification was complete before the bank checked any name, document, or other evidence.','Identity verification began only after the bank checked the customer’s name and documents.','Verification requires checking evidence; it cannot be completed without any check.')],[Q('verification.q1','verification.s1','meaning','What did the bank do before activating the account?','It checked evidence to confirm the customer’s identity.','It guessed the customer’s identity without checking.','It chose a new account name.','Verification is confirmation through examination or evidence.'),Q('verification.q2','verification.s1','context','What is two-step verification meant to do?','Confirm access through an additional check.','Remove every security check.','Rewrite a person’s password aloud.','Verification adds a process for confirming identity or access.'),Q('verification.q3','verification.s1','distinction','Which action is verification?','Comparing a submitted certificate with the issuing record.','Accepting a certificate without inspecting it.','Changing the certificate’s colour.','The comparison checks whether the document is genuine.'),Q('verification.q4','verification.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','verification of the payment details','verdict of the payment details','verbiage of the payment details','Verification is the process of checking details.')]);
P('verify','From Old French verifier, ultimately Latin verificare, “make true,” from verus, “true.”',[C('verify.s1','核实','Please verify the delivery address before submitting the order.','提交訂單前，請核實送貨地址。','verify a fact / address / identity','Verb: check that a fact, document, or figure is correct.','The user checks the address for accuracy.'),C('verify.s2','证实','Independent trials verified the researchers’ prediction about the material.','獨立試驗證實了研究人員對該材料的預測。','verify a claim / theory / result','Verb: show by evidence or testing that a statement is true.','The trials provide evidence for the prediction.')],[M('Please verify the address by deliberately entering a different street from the one on the customer’s record.','Please verify the address by comparing it with the customer’s record.','Entering a conflicting address does not check or confirm the correct one.')],[Q('verify.q1','verify.s1','meaning','What should the customer check before ordering?','That the delivery address is correct.','That the package has already arrived.','That the shop has changed its name.','Verify can mean check a detail for accuracy.'),Q('verify.q2','verify.s2','context','What did the independent trials do?','They supplied evidence supporting the prediction.','They hid the prediction from the researchers.','They changed the material’s address.','Here verify means demonstrate a statement to be true.'),Q('verify.q3','verify.s1','distinction','Which action verifies a passport number?','Compare it with the number on the official document.','Guess a number without seeing the passport.','Replace it with a random number.','Checking the document confirms the number.'),Q('verify.q4','verify.s2','word-choice','Choose the use meaning “prove by testing.”','The experiment verified the proposed mechanism.','The clerk verified the spelling of my surname.','Please verify the meeting room number.','The experiment supplies evidence for the mechanism.')]);
P('vermin','From Anglo-French vermin, from Latin vermis, “worm”; it refers to destructive animals or insects and, insultingly, to people despised as harmful.',[C('vermin.s1','害虫害兽','The grain store was sealed after vermin damaged several sacks of wheat.','害獸破壞了幾袋小麥後，糧倉被封閉起來。','vermin damage / control / infestation','Noun: wild animals or insects that damage crops, food, or buildings.','The animals have harmed stored grain.'),C('vermin.s2','蔑称','The pamphlet dehumanized its opponents by calling them vermin.','那本小冊子把對手稱作害蟲，藉此剝奪他們的人性。','call / treat people as vermin','Noun: an insulting term for people regarded as worthless or disgusting.','The word is used as a dehumanizing insult.')],[M('The farmer called the crop-destroying mice “vermin,” meaning they were skilled legal advisers.','The farmer called the crop-destroying mice “vermin,” meaning they were destructive pests.','Vermin are harmful animals or insects, not legal advisers.')],[Q('vermin.q1','vermin.s1','meaning','Why was the grain store sealed?','Destructive animals had damaged sacks of wheat.','A jury had returned a verdict.','The wheat had been turned into a poem.','Vermin can be animals or insects that damage food.'),Q('vermin.q2','vermin.s2','context','How did the pamphlet use vermin about its opponents?','As a dehumanizing insult.','As a respectful job title.','As a name for a roofed porch.','The people sense is derogatory and treats people as pests.'),Q('vermin.q3','vermin.s1','distinction','Which situation involves vermin in the literal sense?','Rats gnawing through stored grain.','A critic reviewing a film.','A witness answering a jury.','The rats are destructive animals.'),Q('vermin.q4','vermin.s2','word-choice','Which sentence uses the insulting human sense?','The speaker called the targeted group vermin, a dehumanizing slur.','The warehouse hired a company to remove vermin from the grain.','The farmer found vermin in the storage bins.','The first describes the term as an insult against people.')]);
P('vernacular','From Latin vernaculus, “native or domestic,” based on verna, “home-born slave”; it describes a region’s everyday language or a local style.',[C('vernacular.s1','本地日常语言','The guide explained the old proverb in the vernacular spoken by local fishers.','導覽員用當地漁民日常使用的語言解釋這句古諺。','the local / regional vernacular','Noun: the everyday language spoken by ordinary people in a region.','The guide uses the community’s common speech.'),C('vernacular.s2','本地风格的','The new library uses vernacular materials such as local timber and clay tiles.','新圖書館採用地方風格的材料，例如本地木材和陶瓦。','vernacular architecture / design','Adjective: using a local everyday language or characteristic local style.','The materials and design reflect local building traditions.')],[M('The guide explained the proverb in the vernacular, a language that no ordinary resident of the region speaks.','The guide explained the proverb in the vernacular spoken by ordinary residents of the region.','A regional vernacular is the everyday local language, not an unrelated language no one speaks locally.')],[Q('vernacular.q1','vernacular.s1','meaning','Which language did the guide use?','The everyday speech of local fishers.','A language no resident understood.','A set of building materials.','Vernacular can name a region’s ordinary everyday language.'),Q('vernacular.q2','vernacular.s2','context','Why are the library materials called vernacular?','They reflect local building traditions and materials.','They are spoken aloud instead of written.','They are imported from an unrelated region.','The adjective can describe characteristic local style.'),Q('vernacular.q3','vernacular.s1','distinction','What contrasts with a local vernacular in a formal ceremony?','A standardized language used for official settings.','The everyday speech of the same community.','A regional idiom used at home.','Vernacular refers to ordinary local speech.'),Q('vernacular.q4','vernacular.s2','word-choice','Choose the architectural use.','The cottage has vernacular stone walls built in the local style.','The court recorded the jury’s verdict.','The speaker quoted the witness verbatim.','The first describes local architecture.')]);
P('versatile','From Latin versatilis, “turning readily,” from versare, “to turn”; it describes a person adaptable across skills or something useful in many ways.',[C('versatile.s1','多才多艺','A versatile actor can move convincingly from comedy to historical drama.','一位多才多藝的演員能自然地從喜劇轉換到歷史劇。','a versatile performer / worker','Adjective: able to change easily from one skill or activity to another.','The actor succeeds in different kinds of roles.'),C('versatile.s2','多用途的','A versatile kitchen knife can slice vegetables, trim herbs, and portion soft cheese.','一把多用途的廚刀可以切蔬菜、修整香草，也能分切軟起司。','a versatile tool / material','Adjective: having many uses.','The same tool serves several purposes.')],[M('The versatile tool was useful for only one task and could not be adapted to any other use.','The specialized tool was useful for only one task and could not be adapted to any other use.','A versatile object has several uses, unlike a one-purpose tool.')],[Q('versatile.q1','versatile.s1','meaning','Why is the actor versatile?','The actor performs well in different kinds of roles.','The actor can perform only one fixed role.','The actor repairs kitchen knives.','This sense describes adaptability across skills or activities.'),Q('versatile.q2','versatile.s2','context','What makes the knife versatile?','It can perform several kitchen tasks.','It is designed for one use and no others.','It can speak several languages.','A versatile tool has many uses.'),Q('versatile.q3','versatile.s1','distinction','Which employee is versatile?','One trained to handle customer support, scheduling, and reports.','One permitted to do only a single repeated task.','One who owns a multifunctional knife.','The first person works across several skills.'),Q('versatile.q4','versatile.s2','word-choice','Choose the use meaning “useful in many ways.”','A versatile fabric works for curtains, bags, and upholstery.','A versatile pianist performs in several styles.','A versatile actor plays contrasting characters.','The fabric has several practical uses.')]);
P('versatility','From versatile + -ity, from Latin versatilis, “turning readily”; it is the ability to adapt to different skills or uses.',[C('versatility.s1','多面能力；多用途性','The midfielder’s versatility let the coach use her in defence or attack.','這名中場球員的多面能力，讓教練能安排她防守或進攻。','the versatility of a person / tool','Noun: skill in many fields or usefulness for many purposes.','One player can fill different roles.')],[M('The instrument’s versatility meant it could serve one fixed purpose and absolutely no other use.','The instrument’s limited range meant it could serve one fixed purpose and no other use.','Versatility refers to the capacity to adapt or serve multiple purposes.')],[Q('versatility.q1','versatility.s1','meaning','What did the midfielder’s versatility allow?','The coach could use her in different positions.','She could play only one role.','The team could avoid training anyone.','Versatility is the ability to adapt to different roles.'),Q('versatility.q2','versatility.s1','context','Which object demonstrates versatility?','A tool that can tighten screws, cut wire, and open a bottle.','A tool that performs exactly one task.','A tool that is never used.','The first tool has several uses.'),Q('versatility.q3','versatility.s1','distinction','What is versatility in a worker?','Ability to contribute across several kinds of task.','A refusal to learn another task.','A single narrow specialty with no adaptation.','Versatility means broad capability or usefulness.'),Q('versatility.q4','versatility.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','the versatility of the new software','the verdict of the new software','the veranda of the new software','Versatility describes its ability to handle many tasks.')]);
P('verse','From Latin versus, “a line of writing,” from vertere, “turn,” through Old French vers.',[C('verse.s1','诗；韵文','The novel is written in verse, with a rhythmic line pattern rather than ordinary prose.','這部小說以韻文寫成，採用有節奏的詩行，而非一般散文。','write / speak / be in verse','Noun: writing arranged in rhythmic lines, often with rhyme.','The work is poetry rather than ordinary prose.'),C('verse.s2','诗节；歌词段落','The audience joined in when the singer began the second verse.','歌手唱到第二段時，觀眾一起跟唱。','the first / final verse of a song','Noun: a group of lines forming one part of a poem or song.','The singer begins a particular section.')],[M('The second verse of the song was its chorus, repeated unchanged after every verse.','The chorus followed the second verse and was repeated after each verse.','A verse is a section of a song; the repeated chorus is a different section.')],[Q('verse.q1','verse.s1','meaning','How is the novel written?','In rhythmic lines rather than ordinary prose.','As a list of legal decisions.','As an unedited interview transcript.','Verse can mean poetry arranged in lines.'),Q('verse.q2','verse.s2','context','When did the audience join the singer?','At the beginning of the song’s second section.','During the jury’s deliberation.','When a road verge appeared.','A verse can be one section of a song.'),Q('verse.q3','verse.s1','distinction','What does “in verse” contrast with?','In prose','In a spoken agreement','In a vertical line','Verse is rhythmic line writing; prose is ordinary continuous writing.'),Q('verse.q4','verse.s2','word-choice','Choose the song-section use.','The band repeated the final verse before the chorus.','The report quoted the witness verbatim.','The court returned a verdict.','The first names a group of song lines.')]);
P('versed','From Latin versari, “be occupied with or experienced in”; in modern English it is especially used in “well versed in.”',[C('versed.s1','精通的','Our new librarian is well versed in archival cataloguing and old map collections.','我們的新圖書館員精通檔案編目和古地圖收藏。','well versed in + subject / field','Adjective: knowledgeable or skilled through study or experience.','The librarian has expertise in those subjects.')],[M('He was well versed in marine law because he had never studied it and knew nothing about it.','He was unfamiliar with marine law because he had never studied it and knew nothing about it.','Someone who knows nothing about a field is not well versed in it.')],[Q('versed.q1','versed.s1','meaning','What is the librarian well versed in?','Archival cataloguing and old maps.','Repairing aircraft engines.','Writing song lyrics.','Well versed in means knowledgeable or skilled in a subject.'),Q('versed.q2','versed.s1','context','Which person is well versed in tax law?','A lawyer who has studied and practised tax law for years.','A visitor who has never heard of tax law.','A person who only knows the word “tax.”','Study and experience provide the relevant knowledge.'),Q('versed.q3','versed.s1','grammar','Which preposition normally follows versed?','in','at to','of by','The common phrase is well versed in a subject.'),Q('versed.q4','versed.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','She is well versed in the history of the port.','She is well versed at the history of the port.','She is well versed into the history of the port.','The idiomatic construction is versed in.')]);
P('version','From Latin versionem, “a turning or translation,” from vertere, “to turn”; it can be a form, account, or adaptation.',[C('version.s1','版本','The app’s latest version adds offline maps and fixes a security flaw.','這個應用程式的最新版本加入離線地圖，並修補了一項安全漏洞。','the latest / revised version','Noun: a particular form of a book, product, or software.','This release differs from earlier forms.'),C('version.s2','个人说法','Her version of the accident differed from the account recorded by the bus driver.','她對事故的說法與公車司機記錄的情況不同。','someone’s version of events','Noun: one person’s description of what happened.','The two people give different accounts.'),C('version.s3','改编本','The radio version of the novel moves the story from the coast to the mountains.','這部小說的廣播改編版把故事背景從海岸移到了山區。','a film / radio / stage version','Noun: a work adapted for a new purpose or style.','The original story has been changed for radio.')],[M('The radio version was an exact copy in a different medium, with no adaptation or change of any kind.','The radio version adapted the story for a different medium.','A version adapted for radio is a form made for a new medium, not an unchanged physical copy.')],[Q('version.q1','version.s1','meaning','What does the app’s latest version add?','Offline maps and a security fix.','A different witness’s memory.','A radio adaptation of a novel.','This version is a particular software release.'),Q('version.q2','version.s2','context','Why do the accounts differ?','The driver and passenger give different descriptions of the accident.','The app received a software update.','The novel was adapted for radio.','A person’s version is that person’s account.'),Q('version.q3','version.s3','distinction','What is a radio version of a novel?','An adaptation made for radio.','The passenger’s account of an accident.','The newest release of a phone app.','This sense is an adaptation for a new form.'),Q('version.q4','version.s1','word-choice','Choose the software use.','Install version 4.2 to receive the security fix.','Ask each witness for a version of events.','Listen to the radio version of the novel.','Version 4.2 names a software release.')]);
P('versus','From Latin versus, “turned toward or against,” the past participle of vertere, “turn.”',[C('versus.s1','对阵','The final will be North City versus Lakeside in the regional football cup.','區域足球盃決賽將由北城對陣湖濱。','A versus B; team versus team','Preposition: used between two opposing sides in a match or case.','The two named teams face one another.'),C('versus.s2','相比取舍','The committee weighed speed versus reliability before choosing the new system.','委員會在選擇新系統前，權衡了速度與可靠性。','X versus Y; cost versus benefit','Preposition: compared with another option to show a contrast or trade-off.','The committee compares two competing qualities.')],[M('The headline “North City versus Lakeside” said that both teams were cooperating as one side against nobody.','The headline “North City versus Lakeside” announced a match between opposing teams.','Versus marks opposing sides, not two teams acting as one.')],[Q('versus.q1','versus.s1','meaning','What does North City versus Lakeside announce?','A match between the two opposing teams.','A joint team with no opponent.','A software update.','Versus is placed between opposing sides.'),Q('versus.q2','versus.s2','context','What did the committee weigh?','The trade-off between speed and reliability.','The spelling of two team names.','A transcript against a verdict.','This sense compares alternatives or competing qualities.'),Q('versus.q3','versus.s1','distinction','Which use is a legal case label?','State versus Lee','State in Lee','State for Lee','Versus names opposing sides in a legal case.'),Q('versus.q4','versus.s2','word-choice','Choose the comparison use.','The report examines prevention versus treatment.','The semifinal is East versus West.','The lawsuit is Smith versus Jones.','The first compares two policy choices.')]);
P('vertebrate','From Latin vertebratus, “having joints,” from vertebra, “joint of the spine.”',[C('vertebrate.s1','脊椎动物','A salmon is a vertebrate because its skeleton includes a backbone.','鮭魚是脊椎動物，因為牠的骨骼包含脊柱。','a vertebrate animal / species','Noun: an animal with a backbone made of vertebrae.','The fish has a spinal column.'),C('vertebrate.s2','有脊椎的','The biologist compared vertebrate embryos at an early developmental stage.','生物學家比較了有脊椎動物在早期發育階段的胚胎。','vertebrate animals / groups','Adjective: having a backbone or spinal column.','The adjective classifies animals with a backbone.')],[M('A jellyfish is a vertebrate because it has no backbone or spinal column.','A jellyfish is an invertebrate because it has no backbone or spinal column.','An animal without a backbone is not a vertebrate.')],[Q('vertebrate.q1','vertebrate.s1','meaning','Why is a salmon a vertebrate?','Its skeleton includes a backbone.','It has no internal structure.','It is a plant with a stem.','Vertebrates possess a backbone.'),Q('vertebrate.q2','vertebrate.s2','context','What did the biologist compare?','Embryos of animals that have spinal columns.','A set of rocks without animal tissue.','Plants with no roots.','Vertebrate is an adjective for having a backbone.'),Q('vertebrate.q3','vertebrate.s1','distinction','Which animal is a vertebrate?','A frog with a backbone','A jellyfish with no backbone','A sponge with no spinal column','The frog belongs to animals with a spinal column.'),Q('vertebrate.q4','vertebrate.s2','word-choice','Choose the adjective use.','The museum displayed vertebrate fossils from ancient fish.','The vertebrate was kept in a tank.','The spine is a vertebrate.','In the first, vertebrate modifies fossils and means from animals with backbones.')]);
P('vertical','From Late Latin verticalis, “overhead,” from vertex, “top or summit”; it describes an up-and-down line or a hierarchy.',[C('vertical.s1','垂直的','Draw a vertical line from the top of the page to its bottom edge.','從頁面頂端到底邊畫一條垂直線。','a vertical line / wall','Adjective: going straight up at a right angle to a flat base.','The line runs from top to bottom.'),C('vertical.s2','纵向的','The company uses vertical integration to manage several stages of production.','公司採用縱向整合來管理多個生產階段。','vertical integration / control','Adjective: involving different levels within one system or industry.','The company controls stages at different production levels.'),C('vertical.s3','垂直线','The diagram’s vertical is marked with a scale from zero to ten.','圖表的縱軸標有從零到十的刻度。','the vertical; off the vertical','Noun: a line or position that is straight up and down.','The noun names the up-and-down axis.')],[M('The vertical line ran horizontally from the left edge to the right edge of the page.','The horizontal line ran from the left edge to the right edge of the page.','A left-to-right line is horizontal, not vertical.')],[Q('vertical.q1','vertical.s1','meaning','Which direction should the line run?','From the top of the page toward the bottom.','From the left edge to the right edge.','In a circle around the page.','Vertical means straight up and down.'),Q('vertical.q2','vertical.s2','context','What does vertical integration connect?','Different stages or levels of production.','Only firms at the same stage.','A wall to the floor at a right angle.','The business sense concerns control across levels.'),Q('vertical.q3','vertical.s3','distinction','What does “the vertical” name on the diagram?','The up-and-down axis.','A side road’s grassy strip.','The audio recording’s transcript.','As a noun, vertical can name an upright line or position.'),Q('vertical.q4','vertical.s1','word-choice','Choose the geometric use.','The ladder stood against a vertical wall.','The company bought a supplier through vertical integration.','The graph’s vertical is labelled in metres.','The wall orientation is the geometric adjective sense.')]);
P('vertically','From vertical + -ly; it means in an up-and-down direction or arranged from top to bottom.',[C('vertically.s1','垂直地','The lift carries passengers vertically between the ground floor and the roof.','電梯在地面樓層與屋頂之間垂直運送乘客。','move / rise / hang vertically','Adverb: in a direction straight up and down.','The lift travels upward and downward.'),C('vertically.s2','纵向排列','The names are arranged vertically in a column beside the chart.','名字沿著圖表旁的欄位縱向排列。','arrange / stack vertically','Adverb: in a line from top to bottom.','The names form an upright column.')],[M('The lift travelled vertically by moving sideways across the floor without going up or down.','The lift travelled horizontally across the floor without going up or down.','Sideways movement across a floor is horizontal, not vertical.')],[Q('vertically.q1','vertically.s1','meaning','How does the lift move between floors?','Up and down.','Sideways across one floor only.','In a circular orbit around the building.','Vertically describes an up-and-down direction.'),Q('vertically.q2','vertically.s2','context','How are the names arranged?','One below another in a column.','Across a single row from left to right.','In a circle around the chart.','Vertical arrangement runs from top to bottom.'),Q('vertically.q3','vertically.s1','distinction','Which object moves vertically?','A balloon rising straight into the sky.','A train crossing a flat field.','A boat drifting downstream.','The balloon moves upward.'),Q('vertically.q4','vertically.s2','word-choice','Choose the layout phrase.','Stack the boxes vertically, one above another.','Lay the boxes vertically side by side along the floor.','Arrange the boxes verbatim on a page.','Stacking one above another is vertical arrangement.')]);
P('vertigo','From Latin vertigo, “a whirling or dizziness,” from vertere, “to turn.”',[C('vertigo.s1','眩晕','Standing near the unguarded edge gave him vertigo, so he stepped back and sat down.','站在沒有護欄的邊緣附近讓他感到眩暈，因此他退後坐下。','an attack of vertigo; suffer from vertigo','Noun: a feeling that you or your surroundings are spinning, often with loss of balance.','He feels a spinning sensation and moves to safety.')],[M('She called it vertigo even though she felt no spinning sensation and had no balance problem.','She said she felt steady and had no vertigo.','Vertigo specifically involves a spinning sensation, often with loss of balance.')],[Q('vertigo.q1','vertigo.s1','meaning','What did the man feel near the edge?','A spinning sensation that made him step back.','A sudden increase in wind speed.','A legal decision from a jury.','Vertigo is a whirling feeling, often affecting balance.'),Q('vertigo.q2','vertigo.s1','context','Which symptom best fits vertigo?','The room seems to spin while the person struggles to keep balance.','The person has a mild dislike of one food.','The person cannot read a vertical line.','The spinning sensation is characteristic of vertigo.'),Q('vertigo.q3','vertigo.s1','distinction','What makes vertigo more specific than ordinary tiredness?','A sensation of spinning or whirling.','A need for more sleep.','A change in spoken wording.','Vertigo is a spinning sensation, not simply fatigue.'),Q('vertigo.q4','vertigo.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','The height triggered an attack of vertigo.','The height triggered an attack of verbiage.','The height triggered a verdict.','Vertigo names the dizzy spinning feeling.')]);
P('very','From Middle English verray, “true or genuine,” via Old French verai from Latin verus, “true”; it is an intensifier and can mean exact or extreme.',[C('very.s1','非常','The lake was very cold, so the children tested the water before swimming.','湖水非常冷，所以孩子們游泳前先試了水溫。','very + adjective / adverb','Adverb: used before an adjective or adverb to make it stronger.','Very increases the degree of cold.'),C('very.s2','正是；恰好','That is the very key I lost yesterday; its brass tag has my initials.','那正是我昨天弄丟的鑰匙；黃銅吊牌上有我的姓名縮寫。','the very + noun; my very own','Adjective: stresses that this is the exact person or thing meant.','The speaker identifies the exact key.'),C('very.s3','最……的；極端的','At the very end of the tunnel, the rescue team found a narrow exit.','在隧道最盡頭，救援隊找到一個狹窄出口。','the very end / beginning / best','Adjective: marks the furthest or most extreme point.','Very emphasizes the extreme endpoint.')],[M('The water is very freezing because it is exactly at its freezing point.','The water is freezing because it is at its freezing point.','Freezing already expresses an extreme condition; the standard use here is not “very freezing.”')],[Q('very.q1','very.s1','meaning','How cold was the lake?','It was extremely cold.','It was the exact lake the children lost.','It was at the far end of a tunnel.','Very strengthens the adjective cold.'),Q('very.q2','very.s2','context','Why did the speaker call it “the very key”?','It was the exact key that had been lost.','It was one of many unrelated keys.','It was a key made from very cold water.','Very before a noun can emphasize the exact item.'),Q('very.q3','very.s3','distinction','Where was the rescue team’s exit?','At the extreme end of the tunnel.','Near the tunnel entrance only.','In the middle of the lake.','The very end means the furthest endpoint.'),Q('very.q4','very.s1','grammar','Which sentence uses very as an intensifier correctly?','The room was very quiet after the meeting.','The room very became quiet after the meeting.','The very roomly was quiet.','Very normally modifies an adjective such as quiet.')]);

})();
